{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019KQwxb5oMT86HPfAqrnfbj","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Paper Framing — recovery_aware_struct_prune\n2\t\n3\t## Target Venue\n4\t- Primary: EMNLP 2026 Main (ARR May 25 submission)\n5\t- Fallback: EMNLP 2026 Findings\n6\t- Deadline: ARR May 25, 2026\n7\t\n8\t## Core Insight (Redundancy-Stability Tradeoff)\n9\tRLVR alignment (GRPO) fundamentally fails on structurally pruned reasoning models: reward improves but accuracy does not — a pruning-induced reward hacking phenomenon. We show the failure mechanism via **collapse dynamics**: pruning method determines how fast GRPO collapses, and this speed is a diagnostic of structural damage type. Crucially, functional redundancy plays **opposite roles** under SFT vs RLVR recovery:\n10\t\n11\t- **SFT**: redundant structures (high CKA overlap) are safely removable — their function redistributes through gradient-based learning. CKA-aware pruning (RASP) yields marginal SFT advantage.\n12\t- **RLVR**: redundant structures provide **exploration stability** — backup paths that prevent policy collapse during RL. Removing them (as RASP does) accelerates collapse.\n13\t\n14\tThis creates a **Redundancy-Stability Tradeoff**: the structures optimal to prune for SFT recovery are exactly those needed for RLVR stability. Optimal pruning is fundamentally conditioned on the recovery paradigm.\n15\t\n16\t## Core Claims (3) — REVISED based on experimental evidence\n17\t\n18\t1. **GRPO reward-accuracy decoupling is universal; pruning adds training collapse**: GRPO does not improve reasoning accuracy for ANY model post-SFT — unpruned (**81.27% = SFT 81.27%, Δ=0.00pp, identical 1072/1319 correct**), Standard-pruned (58.91% vs 59.29%, Δ=-0.38pp), RASP-pruned (60.65% vs 61.49%, Δ=-0.84pp). Reward increases dramatically (unpruned: 0→0.661) yet accuracy is unchanged — a universal reward-accuracy decoupling under GRPO+GSM8K+greedy. The pruning-specific phenomenon is **training collapse**: RASP collapses permanently at step ~10 (frac_zero_std→0.95, grad→0.007), Standard shows transient dip at step ~60, while unpruned trains stably for 100 steps. GRPO's reward signal does not encode genuine reasoning improvement; pruning removes the structural capacity to even sustain RL training.\n19\t\n20\t2. **Collapse severity gradient diagnoses structural damage**: Three-model comparison reveals a clean severity gradient — RASP (removes redundant, protects unique): permanent collapse step ~10, peak reward 0.039; Standard (importance-only): transient dip step ~60, final reward 0.065; Unpruned: no collapse, final reward 0.661. The 6× speedup from Standard→RASP confirms that functional redundancy provides RLVR exploration stability. Collapse dynamics are a zero-cost diagnostic: fast collapse = aggressive redundancy removal = poor RL trainability.\n21\t\n22\t3. **Recovery method conditions optimal pruning strategy**: For SFT recovery, RASP shows marginal advantage (+2.2pp, RASP 61.49% vs Standard 59.29%, N=1319, p=0.25). For RLVR stability, RASP is actively harmful (6× faster collapse). The structures optimal to prune for SFT are exactly those needed for RLVR stability — a fundamental Redundancy-Stability Tradeoff. Consistent with \"RL Squeezes, SFT Expands\" (ICLR 2026).\n23\t\n24\t## Evidence Status (as of 2026-05-16, ALL CORE DATA COMPLETE)\n25\t\n26\t| Evidence | Status | Result |\n27\t|----------|--------|--------|\n28\t| Unpruned SFT eval (N=1319) | ✅ | 81.27% |\n29\t| Unpruned GRPO step-100 eval (N=1319) | ✅ | **81.27% (Δ=0.00pp, 1072/1319 = identical to SFT)** |\n30\t| Unpruned GRPO step-90 eval (N=1319) | ✅ | **80.59% (1063/1319, confirms stability across late training)** |\n31\t| Standard SFT eval (N=1319) | ✅ | 59.29% |\n32\t| Standard GRPO step-50 eval (N=1319) | ✅ | 58.91% (Δ=-0.38pp) |\n33\t| RASP SFT eval (N=1319) | ✅ | 61.49% |\n34\t| RASP GRPO step-5 eval (N=1319) | ✅ | 60.65% (Δ=-0.84pp) |\n35\t| RASP GRPO v9 collapse dynamics | ✅ | Permanent collapse step ~10, peak reward 0.039 |\n36\t| Standard GRPO v8 dynamics | ✅ | Transient dip step ~60, recovery step ~90 |\n37\t| Unpruned GRPO v2 dynamics | ✅ | No collapse, 100 steps stable, reward 0.661 |\n38\t| Alpha ablation (cal=512) | ✅ | U-shape: α≥1.0 > α≤0.5 post-prune |\n39\t| SFT gap significance | ⚠️ p=0.25 | Not significant at N=1319; scope expansion to higher sparsity planned |\n40\t| RASP GRPO step-10 eval (N=1319) | ✅ | **61.87% — collapse onset does NOT reduce accuracy (vs step-5 60.65%, p=0.52)** |\n41\t\n42\t## Story Spine\n43\t\n44\t- **Problem**: The reasoning model compression pipeline (prune → recover → align) assumes alignment is independent of pruning decisions. We show this assumption fails catastrophically: GRPO alignment on pruned models produces reward improvement without accuracy gain, followed by complete collapse. The pruning-alignment interaction is not merely suboptimal — it is fundamentally broken under current practice.\n45\t\n46\t- **Existing approaches & gaps**: Self-Healing (2025) claims RLVR recovers pruned reasoning models to 95%+ at 25% compression — but uses a single pruning ratio and does not report per-step accuracy during GRPO. GRASPrune (ACL 2026) provides SOTA budgeted structural pruning but doesn't study recovery or alignment at all. RESP (Dec 2025) uses reasoning-trace calibration without recovery. No work has documented GRPO collapse on pruned models, explained its mechanism, or shown that pruning strategy determines collapse dynamics.\n47\t\n48\t- **Our framing**: We present the first systematic study of how structural pruning interacts with RLVR alignment in reasoning LLMs. We introduce RASP (S(h) = I(h) × (1-F(h))^α) not as a universally superior method, but as a **diagnostic tool** that reveals the Redundancy-Stability Tradeoff: CKA-aware structure selection that benefits SFT recovery actively harms RLVR stability. This reframes the pruning-alignment relationship from \"which structures to remove for best recovery\" to \"recovery paradigm determines what counts as safe to remove.\"\n49\t\n50\t- **Headline result**: \"GRPO reward improvement never translates to accuracy gain (unpruned: reward 0→0.661, accuracy 81.27%→81.27%; identical 1072/1319 correct). But pruning causes GRPO training collapse: RASP-pruned collapses permanently at step 10, Standard-pruned at step 60, unpruned never. The severity gradient (RASP > Standard > Unpruned) reveals that structural redundancy — expendable for SFT — provides critical RL exploration stability.\"\n51\t\n52\t## Venue Fit\n53\t- EMNLP Efficient Methods track: structured pruning + reasoning model alignment failure analysis\n54\t- Negative/diagnostic results challenging published claims (Self-Healing) are high-impact at *ACL venues\n55\t- Reasoning model compression pipeline failures are immediately practical (timely: DeepSeek-R1, QwQ, Kimi-K1.5)\n56\t- Mechanistic analysis (collapse dynamics, reward-accuracy divergence) aligns with EMNLP empirical rigor\n57\t\n58\t## Venue Fit Risks\n59\t- **\"Just a negative result without solution\"**: Mitigate with (1) mechanistic explanation (redundancy-stability tradeoff), (2) RASP as diagnostic tool (collapse speed predicts pruning quality for RL), (3) actionable implication (SFT-only recovery is currently the safe path; RLVR needs pruning-aware modifications)\n60\t- **\"Single model\"**: DeepSeek-R1-Distill-Qwen-7B is the canonical open reasoning model; multi-method comparison (RASP/Standard/Unpruned) + multi-recovery (SFT/GRPO) compensates\n61\t- **\"GRPO config might be wrong\"**: Report hyperparameter sensitivity (alpha ablation), show collapse is robust across configs, cite Self-Healing uses similar GRPO setup\n62\t- **\"SFT gap not significant\"**: Frame honestly as marginal; the paper's contribution is the GRPO failure + mechanism, not the SFT comparison. SFT gap is supplementary context.\n63\t- **\"Collapse might be training instability, not pruning-specific\"**: Unpruned GRPO ran 100 steps with zero collapse (reward 0.661, stable frac_zero_std ≤0.275) — pruning-specificity confirmed\n64\t\n65\t## Anticipated Reviewer Concerns & Experimental Responses\n66\t\n67\t| Concern | Response | Supporting Experiment |\n68\t|---------|----------|----------------------|\n69\t| GRPO failure might be hyperparameter issue | Alpha ablation shows U-shape is robust; reward increases but accuracy never follows | alpha_ablation_sweep |\n70\t| Need unpruned control for pruning-specificity | Unpruned GRPO: 100 steps stable, no collapse, reward 0.661 vs pruned collapse at step 10-60 | grpo_unpruned_v2 |\n71\t| SFT gap not significant | Acknowledged; paper's main claim is GRPO failure, not SFT superiority | sft_eval N=1319 |\n72\t| Collapse speed might not generalize | Multi-method comparison (RASP/Standard) + multi-config (alpha sweep) | grpo_v8, grpo_v9 |\n73\t| How does this relate to Self-Healing claims? | Self-Healing uses 25% unstructured; our structured pruning at 20% creates different damage pattern | Discussion section |\n74\t| What's the practical recommendation? | SFT recovery only for structurally pruned models; RLVR requires pruning-aware alignment (future work) | All experiments |\n75\t| CKA-aware pruning hurts RLVR — why publish RASP? | RASP is the diagnostic tool that REVEALS the tradeoff; its failure under RLVR is the evidence | grpo_v9 vs grpo_v8 |\n76\t\n77\t## Key Differentiations\n78\t- **vs Self-Healing (2025)**: Claims RLVR recovers pruned models → we show GRPO fails (reward hacking + collapse); different pruning granularity and controlled collapse analysis\n79\t- **vs MPruner (2024)**: inter-layer CKA for depth pruning in CNNs → we use intra-layer CKA as diagnostic tool revealing redundancy-stability tradeoff in reasoning LLMs\n80\t- **vs GRASPrune (ACL 2026)**: SOTA budgeted pruning without recovery/alignment study → we study the full prune-recover-align pipeline failure\n81\t- **vs RESP (Dec 2025)**: reasoning-trace calibration without recovery → we study recovery paradigm interaction\n82\t- **vs PASER (2025)**: optimizes recovery DATA → we show even optimal pruning STRUCTURE cannot save RLVR alignment\n83\t\n84\t## Open Questions (scope expansion experiments planned)\n85\t1. ~~Does unpruned model also show reward-accuracy divergence?~~ → YES, confirmed: 81.27% = 81.27%\n86\t2. ~~What do RASP v9 fine-grained checkpoints show?~~ → Permanent collapse, step-5 eval = 60.65% (≈ SFT)\n87\t3. Can higher sparsity (25-30%) make SFT gap significant AND intensify GRPO collapse? (scope expansion Phase 1)\n88\t4. Does the collapse pattern reproduce on Qwen2.5-Math-7B? (scope expansion Phase 2)\n89\t5. Is there a GRPO config that avoids collapse on pruned models? (future work motivation)\n90\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"382d3fca-c918-4d79-9064-e8f82775e1fe","uuid":"f7261fa7-72ac-4bd1-898f-285c4bdfe7f5","timestamp":"2026-05-16T15:24:39.340Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_17/projects/recovery_aware_struct_prune/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260516T144805/worst/paper_framing.md","content":"# Paper Framing — recovery_aware_struct_prune\n\n## Target Venue\n- Primary: EMNLP 2026 Main (ARR May 25 submission)\n- Fallback: EMNLP 2026 Findings\n- Deadline: ARR May 25, 2026\n\n## Core Insight (Redundancy-Stability Tradeoff)\nRLVR alignment (GRPO) fundamentally fails on structurally pruned reasoning models: reward improves but accuracy does not — a pruning-induced reward hacking phenomenon. We show the failure mechanism via **collapse dynamics**: pruning method determines how fast GRPO collapses, and this speed is a diagnostic of structural damage type. Crucially, functional redundancy plays **opposite roles** under SFT vs RLVR recovery:\n\n- **SFT**: redundant structures (high CKA overlap) are safely removable — their function redistributes through gradient-based learning. CKA-aware pruning (RASP) yields marginal SFT advantage.\n- **RLVR**: redundant structures provide **exploration stability** — backup paths that prevent policy collapse during RL. Removing them (as RASP does) accelerates collapse.\n\nThis creates a **Redundancy-Stability Tradeoff**: the structures optimal to prune for SFT recovery are exactly those needed for RLVR stability. Optimal pruning is fundamentally conditioned on the recovery paradigm.\n\n## Core Claims (3) — REVISED based on experimental evidence\n\n1. **GRPO reward-accuracy decoupling is universal; pruning adds training collapse**: GRPO does not improve reasoning accuracy for ANY model post-SFT — unpruned (**81.27% = SFT 81.27%, Δ=0.00pp, identical 1072/1319 correct**), Standard-pruned (58.91% vs 59.29%, Δ=-0.38pp), RASP-pruned (60.65% vs 61.49%, Δ=-0.84pp). Reward increases dramatically (unpruned: 0→0.661) yet accuracy is unchanged — a universal reward-accuracy decoupling under GRPO+GSM8K+greedy. The pruning-specific phenomenon is **training collapse**: RASP collapses permanently at step ~10 (frac_zero_std→0.95, grad→0.007), Standard shows transient dip at step ~60, while unpruned trains stably for 100 steps. GRPO's reward signal does not encode genuine reasoning improvement; pruning removes the structural capacity to even sustain RL training.\n\n2. **Collapse severity gradient diagnoses structural damage**: Three-model comparison reveals a clean severity gradient — RASP (removes redundant, protects unique): permanent collapse step ~10, peak reward 0.039; Standard (importance-only): transient dip step ~60, final reward 0.065; Unpruned: no collapse, final reward 0.661. The 6× speedup from Standard→RASP confirms that functional redundancy provides RLVR exploration stability. Collapse dynamics are a zero-cost diagnostic: fast collapse = aggressive redundancy removal = poor RL trainability.\n\n3. **Recovery method conditions optimal pruning strategy**: For SFT recovery, RASP shows marginal advantage (+2.2pp, RASP 61.49% vs Standard 59.29%, N=1319, p=0.25). For RLVR stability, RASP is actively harmful (6× faster collapse). The structures optimal to prune for SFT are exactly those needed for RLVR stability — a fundamental Redundancy-Stability Tradeoff. Consistent with \"RL Squeezes, SFT Expands\" (ICLR 2026).\n\n## Evidence Status (as of 2026-05-16, ALL CORE DATA COMPLETE)\n\n| Evidence | Status | Result |\n|----------|--------|--------|\n| Unpruned SFT eval (N=1319) | ✅ | 81.27% |\n| Unpruned GRPO step-100 eval (N=1319) | ✅ | **81.27% (Δ=0.00pp, 1072/1319 = identical to SFT)** |\n| Unpruned GRPO step-90 eval (N=1319) | ✅ | **80.59% (1063/1319, confirms stability across late training)** |\n| Standard SFT eval (N=1319) | ✅ | 59.29% |\n| Standard GRPO step-50 eval (N=1319) | ✅ | 58.91% (Δ=-0.38pp) |\n| RASP SFT eval (N=1319) | ✅ | 61.49% |\n| RASP GRPO step-5 eval (N=1319) | ✅ | 60.65% (Δ=-0.84pp) |\n| RASP GRPO v9 collapse dynamics | ✅ | Permanent collapse step ~10, peak reward 0.039 |\n| Standard GRPO v8 dynamics | ✅ | Transient dip step ~60, recovery step ~90 |\n| Unpruned GRPO v2 dynamics | ✅ | No collapse, 100 steps stable, reward 0.661 |\n| Alpha ablation (cal=512) | ✅ | U-shape: α≥1.0 > α≤0.5 post-prune |\n| SFT gap significance | ⚠️ p=0.25 | Not significant at N=1319; scope expansion to higher sparsity planned |\n| RASP GRPO step-10 eval (N=1319) | ✅ | **61.87% — collapse onset does NOT reduce accuracy (vs step-5 60.65%, p=0.52)** |\n\n## Story Spine\n\n- **Problem**: The reasoning model compression pipeline (prune → recover → align) assumes alignment is independent of pruning decisions. We show this assumption fails catastrophically: GRPO alignment on pruned models produces reward improvement without accuracy gain, followed by complete collapse. The pruning-alignment interaction is not merely suboptimal — it is fundamentally broken under current practice.\n\n- **Existing approaches & gaps**: Self-Healing (2025) claims RLVR recovers pruned reasoning models to 95%+ at 25% compression — but uses a single pruning ratio and does not report per-step accuracy during GRPO. GRASPrune (ACL 2026) provides SOTA budgeted structural pruning but doesn't study recovery or alignment at all. RESP (Dec 2025) uses reasoning-trace calibration without recovery. No work has documented GRPO collapse on pruned models, explained its mechanism, or shown that pruning strategy determines collapse dynamics.\n\n- **Our framing**: We present the first systematic study of how structural pruning interacts with RLVR alignment in reasoning LLMs. We introduce RASP (S(h) = I(h) × (1-F(h))^α) not as a universally superior method, but as a **diagnostic tool** that reveals the Redundancy-Stability Tradeoff: CKA-aware structure selection that benefits SFT recovery actively harms RLVR stability. This reframes the pruning-alignment relationship from \"which structures to remove for best recovery\" to \"recovery paradigm determines what counts as safe to remove.\"\n\n- **Headline result**: \"GRPO reward improvement never translates to accuracy gain (unpruned: reward 0→0.661, accuracy 81.27%→81.27%; identical 1072/1319 correct). But pruning causes GRPO training collapse: RASP-pruned collapses permanently at step 10, Standard-pruned at step 60, unpruned never. The severity gradient (RASP > Standard > Unpruned) reveals that structural redundancy — expendable for SFT — provides critical RL exploration stability.\"\n\n## Venue Fit\n- EMNLP Efficient Methods track: structured pruning + reasoning model alignment failure analysis\n- Negative/diagnostic results challenging published claims (Self-Healing) are high-impact at *ACL venues\n- Reasoning model compression pipeline failures are immediately practical (timely: DeepSeek-R1, QwQ, Kimi-K1.5)\n- Mechanistic analysis (collapse dynamics, reward-accuracy divergence) aligns with EMNLP empirical rigor\n\n## Venue Fit Risks\n- **\"Just a negative result without solution\"**: Mitigate with (1) mechanistic explanation (redundancy-stability tradeoff), (2) RASP as diagnostic tool (collapse speed predicts pruning quality for RL), (3) actionable implication (SFT-only recovery is currently the safe path; RLVR needs pruning-aware modifications)\n- **\"Single model\"**: DeepSeek-R1-Distill-Qwen-7B is the canonical open reasoning model; multi-method comparison (RASP/Standard/Unpruned) + multi-recovery (SFT/GRPO) compensates\n- **\"GRPO config might be wrong\"**: Report hyperparameter sensitivity (alpha ablation), show collapse is robust across configs, cite Self-Healing uses similar GRPO setup\n- **\"SFT gap not significant\"**: Frame honestly as marginal; the paper's contribution is the GRPO failure + mechanism, not the SFT comparison. SFT gap is supplementary context.\n- **\"Collapse might be training instability, not pruning-specific\"**: Unpruned GRPO ran 100 steps with zero collapse (reward 0.661, stable frac_zero_std ≤0.275) — pruning-specificity confirmed\n\n## Anticipated Reviewer Concerns & Experimental Responses\n\n| Concern | Response | Supporting Experiment |\n|---------|----------|----------------------|\n| GRPO failure might be hyperparameter issue | Alpha ablation shows U-shape is robust; reward increases but accuracy never follows | alpha_ablation_sweep |\n| Need unpruned control for pruning-specificity | Unpruned GRPO: 100 steps stable, no collapse, reward 0.661 vs pruned collapse at step 10-60 | grpo_unpruned_v2 |\n| SFT gap not significant | Acknowledged; paper's main claim is GRPO failure, not SFT superiority | sft_eval N=1319 |\n| Collapse speed might not generalize | Multi-method comparison (RASP/Standard) + multi-config (alpha sweep) | grpo_v8, grpo_v9 |\n| How does this relate to Self-Healing claims? | Self-Healing uses 25% unstructured; our structured pruning at 20% creates different damage pattern | Discussion section |\n| What's the practical recommendation? | SFT recovery only for structurally pruned models; RLVR requires pruning-aware alignment (future work) | All experiments |\n| CKA-aware pruning hurts RLVR — why publish RASP? | RASP is the diagnostic tool that REVEALS the tradeoff; its failure under RLVR is the evidence | grpo_v9 vs grpo_v8 |\n\n## Key Differentiations\n- **vs Self-Healing (2025)**: Claims RLVR recovers pruned models → we show GRPO fails (reward hacking + collapse); different pruning granularity and controlled collapse analysis\n- **vs MPruner (2024)**: inter-layer CKA for depth pruning in CNNs → we use intra-layer CKA as diagnostic tool revealing redundancy-stability tradeoff in reasoning LLMs\n- **vs GRASPrune (ACL 2026)**: SOTA budgeted pruning without recovery/alignment study → we study the full prune-recover-align pipeline failure\n- **vs RESP (Dec 2025)**: reasoning-trace calibration without recovery → we study recovery paradigm interaction\n- **vs PASER (2025)**: optimizes recovery DATA → we show even optimal pruning STRUCTURE cannot save RLVR alignment\n\n## Open Questions (scope expansion experiments planned)\n1. ~~Does unpruned model also show reward-accuracy divergence?~~ → YES, confirmed: 81.27% = 81.27%\n2. ~~What do RASP v9 fine-grained checkpoints show?~~ → Permanent collapse, step-5 eval = 60.65% (≈ SFT)\n3. Can higher sparsity (25-30%) make SFT gap significant AND intensify GRPO collapse? (scope expansion Phase 1)\n4. Does the collapse pattern reproduce on Qwen2.5-Math-7B? (scope expansion Phase 2)\n5. Is there a GRPO config that avoids collapse on pruned models? (future work motivation)\n","numLines":90,"startLine":1,"totalLines":90}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NE7gv8QyA2qiZ6TqYpRpN8","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t[\n2\t  {\n3\t    \"name\": \"Full GSM8K Eval Baseline + RASP_20 + Standard_20\",\n4\t    \"description\": \"Full test set (N=1319) eval for all three conditions at 20% sparsity\",\n5\t    \"results\": {\n6\t      \"unpruned_accuracy\": 0.8127,\n7\t      \"rasp_20_post_prune_accuracy\": 0.31,\n8\t      \"standard_20_post_prune_accuracy\": 0.27,\n9\t      \"rasp_vs_standard_gap_pp\": 4.0,\n10\t      \"rasp_vs_standard_p_value\": 0.38,\n11\t      \"ci_width_pp\": 2.5\n12\t    },\n13\t    \"tables\": [\n14\t      {\n15\t        \"name\": \"Table: Post-prune accuracy (N=1319)\",\n16\t        \"rows\": [\n17\t          {\n18\t            \"method\": \"Unpruned\",\n19\t            \"accuracy\": \"81.27%\",\n20\t            \"stderr\": \"±1.07pp\"\n21\t          },\n22\t          {\n23\t            \"method\": \"RASP-20%\",\n24\t            \"accuracy\": \"30.5%\",\n25\t            \"stderr\": \"±2.54pp\"\n26\t          },\n27\t          {\n28\t            \"method\": \"Standard-20%\",\n29\t            \"accuracy\": \"27.1%\",\n30\t            \"stderr\": \"±2.45pp\"\n31\t          }\n32\t        ]\n33\t      }\n34\t    ],\n35\t    \"figures\": [],\n36\t    \"analysis\": \"Post-prune gap不显著，不能claim RASP preserves more reasoning capacity pre-recovery。两者都严重degraded到接近random baseline (GSM8K ≈ 0% for truly random)。\\n\\n已有N=100数据(RASP 31% vs Standard 27%)在full eval下只能微幅收敛。4pp gap在N=1319下仍不显著(p≈0.38)，因为post-prune accuracy本身variance大、两者都在random-ish低准确率区间。Worst档下这个gap不构成meaningful difference。\"\n37\t  },\n38\t  {\n39\t    \"name\": \"Full GSM8K Eval All Recovered Models\",\n40\t    \"description\": \"N=1319 eval for SFT-recovered and GRPO-recovered models (RASP_20, Standard_20, unpruned)\",\n41\t    \"results\": {\n42\t      \"sft_rasp_20_accuracy\": 0.6149,\n43\t      \"sft_standard_20_accuracy\": 0.5929,\n44\t      \"sft_gap_20_pp\": 2.2,\n45\t      \"sft_gap_20_p_value\": 0.25,\n46\t      \"grpo_rasp_step5_accuracy\": 0.6065,\n47\t      \"grpo_standard_step50_accuracy\": 0.5891,\n48\t      \"grpo_unpruned_step100_accuracy\": 0.8127,\n49\t      \"grpo_unpruned_delta_vs_sft\": 0.0\n50\t    },\n51\t    \"tables\": [\n52\t      {\n53\t        \"name\": \"Table 1: Recovery accuracy comparison (N=1319)\",\n54\t        \"rows\": [\n55\t          {\n56\t            \"condition\": \"Unpruned SFT\",\n57\t            \"accuracy\": \"81.27%\",\n58\t            \"grpo_accuracy\": \"81.27%\",\n59\t            \"delta\": \"0.00pp\"\n60\t          },\n61\t          {\n62\t            \"condition\": \"RASP-20% SFT\",\n63\t            \"accuracy\": \"61.49%\",\n64\t            \"grpo_accuracy\": \"60.65%\",\n65\t            \"delta\": \"-0.84pp\"\n66\t          },\n67\t          {\n68\t            \"condition\": \"Standard-20% SFT\",\n69\t            \"accuracy\": \"59.29%\",\n70\t            \"grpo_accuracy\": \"58.91%\",\n71\t            \"delta\": \"-0.38pp\"\n72\t          }\n73\t        ]\n74\t      }\n75\t    ],\n76\t    \"figures\": [],\n77\t    \"analysis\": \"Universal reward-accuracy decoupling confirmed。但SFT gap (RASP vs Standard) 在p=0.25下insufficient to support Redundancy-Stability Tradeoff claim。论文只能claim GRPO failure是universal，而非pruning-method-specific。\\n\\n这些数据已实际收集完毕。SFT gap 2.2pp (p=0.25)在worst档下被视为不显著。GRPO对所有模型都不提升accuracy（unpruned: 0.00pp, Standard: -0.38pp, RASP: -0.84pp），这是strong negative result但不需要RASP-specific解释。Collapse dynamics差异（RASP step10 vs Standard step60）在20%下存在，但worst档的核心问题是这个gradient在25%下消失。\"\n78\t  },\n79\t  {\n80\t    \"name\": \"GRASPrune Baseline 20% Sparsity\",\n81\t    \"description\": \"GRASPrune (ACL 2026 SOTA) at 20% sparsity: prune → eval → SFT → GRPO full pipeline\",\n82\t    \"results\": {\n83\t      \"grasp_post_prune_accuracy\": 0.07,\n84\t      \"grasp_post_sft_accuracy\": 0.41,\n85\t      \"grasp_post_grpo_step30_accuracy\": 0.39,\n86\t      \"grasp_grpo_collapse_step\": 5,\n87\t      \"grasp_grpo_final_reward\": 0.012,\n88\t      \"grasp_grpo_frac_zero_std_final\": 0.97\n89\t    },\n90\t    \"tables\": [\n91\t      {\n92\t        \"name\": \"Table: GRASPrune pipeline comparison\",\n93\t        \"rows\": [\n94\t          {\n95\t            \"stage\": \"Post-prune\",\n96\t            \"grasp\": \"7%\",\n97\t            \"rasp\": \"31%\",\n98\t            \"standard\": \"27%\"\n99\t          },\n100\t          {\n101\t            \"stage\": \"Post-SFT\",\n102\t            \"grasp\": \"41%\",\n103\t            \"rasp\": \"61.5%\",\n104\t            \"standard\": \"59.3%\"\n105\t          },\n106\t          {\n107\t            \"stage\": \"Post-GRPO\",\n108\t            \"grasp\": \"39%\",\n109\t            \"rasp\": \"60.7%\",\n110\t            \"standard\": \"58.9%\"\n111\t          },\n112\t          {\n113\t            \"stage\": \"GRPO collapse step\",\n114\t            \"grasp\": \"~5\",\n115\t            \"rasp\": \"~10\",\n116\t            \"standard\": \"~60\"\n117\t          }\n118\t        ]\n119\t      }\n120\t    ],\n121\t    \"figures\": [],\n122\t    \"analysis\": \"GRASPrune数据confirms所有structured pruning methods的GRPO都fail，但severity ordering (GRASPrune < RASP < Standard)在worst档下被解释为trivially correlated with post-SFT quality而非redundancy-specific mechanism。Reviewer会argue: 'collapse speed simply tracks model quality, not structural damage type'。\\n\\nGRASPrune在post-prune (7%)和post-SFT (41%)都远低于RASP(31%→61%)和Standard(27%→59%)。这是因为GRASPrune的gate-based selection在reasoning model上suboptimal——它优化一般loss而非reasoning trace。在worst档下，GRASPrune GRPO会比RASP更快collapse(step 5)，但这不提供diagnostic value因为GRASPrune本身就是inferior pruning，collapse快是trivial结论。这个baseline反而削弱了RASP的novelty——如果所有结构化剪枝方法的GRPO都collapse，那collapse不是RASP-specific insight。\"\n123\t  },\n124\t  {\n125\t    \"name\": \"Multi-seed Post-prune Eval\",\n126\t    \"description\": \"5 seeds (incl. seed 42) for RASP_20 + Standard_20 post-prune eval, variance estimation\",\n127\t    \"results\": {\n128\t      \"rasp_20_mean_accuracy\": 0.305,\n129\t      \"rasp_20_std\": 0.018,\n130\t      \"standard_20_mean_accuracy\": 0.278,\n131\t      \"standard_20_std\": 0.022,\n132\t      \"mean_gap_pp\": 2.7,\n133\t      \"paired_t_p_value\": 0.15,\n134\t      \"cohens_d\": 0.42\n135\t    },\n136\t    \"tables\": [\n137\t      {\n138\t        \"name\": \"Table: Multi-seed post-prune accuracy\",\n139\t        \"rows\": [\n140\t          {\n141\t            \"seed\": 42,\n142\t            \"rasp\": \"31%\",\n143\t            \"standard\": \"27%\"\n144\t          },\n145\t          {\n146\t            \"seed\": 123,\n147\t            \"rasp\": \"29%\",\n148\t            \"standard\": \"28%\"\n149\t          },\n150\t          {\n151\t            \"seed\": 456,\n152\t            \"rasp\": \"32%\",\n153\t            \"standard\": \"30%\"\n154\t          },\n155\t          {\n156\t            \"seed\": 789,\n157\t            \"rasp\": \"28%\",\n158\t            \"standard\": \"26%\"\n159\t          },\n160\t          {\n161\t            \"seed\": 1024,\n162\t            \"rasp\": \"32.5%\",\n163\t            \"standard\": \"28%\"\n164\t          }\n165\t        ]\n166\t      }\n167\t    ],\n168\t    \"figures\": [],\n169\t    \"analysis\": \"Multi-seed证据weak。Gap存在但不robust (p=0.15)。在worst档下这strengthens the narrative that CKA-aware scoring的marginal benefit不justify方法复杂度。\\n\\nPost-prune accuracy受calibration sample variance影响。5 seeds下RASP mean ≈ 30.5%, Standard mean ≈ 27.8%, gap ~2.7pp。但std较大(1.8-2.2pp)导致paired-t test p≈0.15。Worst档下reviewers会argue这个gap不足以支持CKA-aware scoring的优越性。Cohen's d=0.42 (medium effect)不够convincing for a core method claim。\"\n170\t  },\n171\t  {\n172\t    \"name\": \"Scoring Ablation (magnitude/gradient/random)\",\n173\t    \"description\": \"Ablation: magnitude-only, gradient-only, random pruning at 20% sparsity\",\n174\t    \"results\": {\n175\t      \"magnitude_only_accuracy\": 0.26,\n176\t      \"gradient_only_accuracy\": 0.29,\n177\t      \"random_pruning_accuracy\": 0.18,\n178\t      \"rasp_accuracy_ref\": 0.31,\n179\t      \"standard_accuracy_ref\": 0.27,\n180\t      \"gradient_vs_rasp_gap\": 2.0,\n181\t      \"gradient_vs_rasp_p_value\": 0.41\n182\t    },\n183\t    \"tables\": [\n184\t      {\n185\t        \"name\": \"Table: Scoring method ablation (20% sparsity, N=100)\",\n186\t        \"rows\": [\n187\t          {\n188\t            \"method\": \"RASP (I×(1-F)^α)\",\n189\t            \"accuracy\": \"31%\",\n190\t            \"stderr\": \"±4.6%\"\n191\t          },\n192\t          {\n193\t            \"method\": \"Gradient-only (I)\",\n194\t            \"accuracy\": \"29%\",\n195\t            \"stderr\": \"±4.5%\"\n196\t          },\n197\t          {\n198\t            \"method\": \"Standard (importance)\",\n199\t            \"accuracy\": \"27%\",\n200\t            \"stderr\": \"±4.4%\"\n201\t          },\n202\t          {\n203\t            \"method\": \"Magnitude-only\",\n204\t            \"accuracy\": \"26%\",\n205\t            \"stderr\": \"±4.4%\"\n206\t          },\n207\t          {\n208\t            \"method\": \"Random\",\n209\t            \"accuracy\": \"18%\",\n210\t            \"stderr\": \"±3.8%\"\n211\t          }\n212\t        ]\n213\t      }\n214\t    ],\n215\t    \"figures\": [],\n216\t    \"analysis\": \"CKA modulation的贡献被noise淹没。Worst档叙事：RASP's CKA component is at best marginal (2pp over gradient-only, p=0.41)。不足以支持CKA作为method contribution。\\n\\nWorst档下，gradient-only(即Standard的核心——importance scoring)已达到29%，接近RASP的31%。CKA modulation仅额外贡献~2pp，这在N=100下完全不显著(p=0.41)。Magnitude-only(26%)和Standard(27%)几乎相同，说明importance metric差异在post-prune这个极低accuracy regime下noise-dominated。Random(18%)是唯一clearly worse的，但这是trivial——任何informed method都应该beat random。Ablation结果undermine CKA的独立贡献。\"\n217\t  },\n218\t  {\n219\t    \"name\": \"Per-structure CKA-Recoverability Correlation\",\n220\t    \"description\": \"Per-head F(h) vs activation change after recovery, mixed-effects regression\",\n221\t    \"results\": {\n222\t      \"pearson_r_fh_vs_activation_change\": 0.12,\n223\t      \"spearman_rho\": 0.09,\n224\t      \"mixed_effects_p_value_fh\": 0.31,\n225\t      \"variance_explained_by_fh\": 0.014,\n226\t      \"weight_norm_variance_explained\": 0.08,\n227\t      \"gradient_importance_variance_explained\": 0.11\n228\t    },\n229\t    \"tables\": [\n230\t      {\n231\t        \"name\": \"Table: Mixed-effects regression coefficients\",\n232\t        \"rows\": [\n233\t          {\n234\t            \"predictor\": \"F(h) (CKA redundancy)\",\n235\t            \"beta\": \"0.034\",\n236\t            \"p_value\": \"0.31\",\n237\t            \"R²_partial\": \"0.014\"\n238\t          },\n239\t          {\n240\t            \"predictor\": \"Weight norm\",\n241\t            \"beta\": \"0.089\",\n242\t            \"p_value\": \"0.02\",\n243\t            \"R²_partial\": \"0.08\"\n244\t          },\n245\t          {\n246\t            \"predictor\": \"Gradient importance\",\n247\t            \"beta\": \"0.102\",\n248\t            \"p_value\": \"0.008\",\n249\t            \"R²_partial\": \"0.11\"\n250\t          },\n251\t          {\n252\t            \"predictor\": \"Activation magnitude\",\n253\t            \"beta\": \"0.076\",\n254\t            \"p_value\": \"0.04\",\n255\t            \"R²_partial\": \"0.06\"\n256\t          }\n257\t        ]\n258\t      }\n259\t    ],\n260\t    \"figures\": [],\n261\t    \"analysis\": \"CKA-based redundancy metric不predict recovery behavior。在worst档下这是致命的——RASP的理论基础(redundant structures are safely removable for SFT)没有per-structure evidence支撑。\\n\\nWorst档下，F(h)（CKA-based functional redundancy）与recovery后的activation change几乎无correlation (r=0.12)。Mixed-effects model中F(h)不显著(p=0.31)，且解释方差仅1.4%——远低于简单的weight norm (8%)或gradient importance (11%)。这demolishes CKA作为'predicting recoverability'的诊断工具的claim。如果functional redundancy不predict recoverability，Redundancy-Stability Tradeoff的机制基础就不存在。\"\n262\t  },\n263\t  {\n264\t    \"name\": \"SFT-only Recovery Comparison\",\n265\t    \"description\": \"Same pruned models (RASP_20, Standard_20), SFT only, same data budget. Tests recovery paradigm interaction.\",\n266\t    \"results\": {\n267\t      \"sft_rasp_20_accuracy\": 0.6149,\n268\t      \"sft_standard_20_accuracy\": 0.5929,\n269\t      \"sft_gap_pp\": 2.2,\n270\t      \"sft_gap_p_value\": 0.25,\n271\t      \"sft_rasp_loss_curve_final\": 0.64,\n272\t      \"sft_standard_loss_curve_final\": 0.64\n273\t    },\n274\t    \"tables\": [\n275\t      {\n276\t        \"name\": \"Table: SFT-only recovery (N=1319)\",\n277\t        \"rows\": [\n278\t          {\n279\t            \"method\": \"RASP-20%\",\n280\t            \"sft_accuracy\": \"61.49%\",\n281\t            \"sft_loss\": \"0.64\"\n282\t          },\n283\t          {\n284\t            \"method\": \"Standard-20%\",\n285\t            \"sft_accuracy\": \"59.29%\",\n286\t            \"sft_loss\": \"0.64\"\n287\t          },\n288\t          {\n289\t            \"method\": \"Gap\",\n290\t            \"delta\": \"+2.20pp\",\n291\t            \"p_value\": \"0.25\"\n292\t          }\n293\t        ]\n294\t      }\n295\t    ],\n296\t    \"figures\": [],\n297\t    \"analysis\": \"SFT gap不显著。Worst档叙事：无法claim RASP对SFT recovery有advantage，因此Redundancy-Stability Tradeoff的一侧(SFT favors RASP)不成立。\\n\\n这个实验实际上已经完成（plan_002的SFT就是SFT-only recovery）。Worst档下结果不变：RASP 61.49% vs Standard 59.29%，gap 2.2pp, p=0.25。Loss curves几乎identical（都converge到0.64）。不显著的SFT gap意味着'CKA-aware pruning benefits SFT recovery'这个claim不成立。如果SFT gap都不存在，Redundancy-Stability Tradeoff（SFT favors removing redundancy, RLVR needs it）的SFT侧就是null。\"\n298\t  },\n299\t  {\n300\t    \"name\": \"25% Sparsity RASP + Standard Full Pipeline\",\n301\t    \"description\": \"25% sparsity: prune → eval → SFT → GRPO for both RASP and Standard\",\n302\t    \"results\": {\n303\t      \"rasp_25_post_prune_accuracy\": 0.21,\n304\t      \"standard_25_post_prune_accuracy\": 0.16,\n305\t      \"rasp_25_sft_accuracy\": 0.52,\n306\t      \"standard_25_sft_accuracy\": 0.5125,\n307\t      \"sft_gap_25_pp\": 0.75,\n308\t      \"sft_gap_25_p_value\": 0.35,\n309\t      \"grpo_rasp_25_collapse_step\": 4,\n310\t      \"grpo_standard_25_collapse_step\": 6,\n311\t      \"grpo_rasp_25_peak_reward\": 0.011,\n312\t      \"grpo_standard_25_peak_reward\": 0.015,\n313\t      \"grpo_rasp_25_final_frac_zero_std\": 0.98,\n314\t      \"grpo_standard_25_final_frac_zero_std\": 0.96,\n315\t      \"collapse_ratio_rasp_vs_standard\": 0.67\n316\t    },\n317\t    \"tables\": [\n318\t      {\n319\t        \"name\": \"Table: 25% sparsity pipeline comparison\",\n320\t        \"rows\": [\n321\t          {\n322\t            \"stage\": \"Post-prune\",\n323\t            \"rasp_25\": \"21%\",\n324\t            \"standard_25\": \"16%\"\n325\t          },\n326\t          {\n327\t            \"stage\": \"Post-SFT\",\n328\t            \"rasp_25\": \"52%\",\n329\t            \"standard_25\": \"51.25%\"\n330\t          },\n331\t          {\n332\t            \"stage\": \"Post-SFT gap\",\n333\t            \"delta\": \"+0.75pp\",\n334\t            \"p_value\": \"0.35\"\n335\t          },\n336\t          {\n337\t            \"stage\": \"GRPO collapse step\",\n338\t            \"rasp_25\": \"~4\",\n339\t            \"standard_25\": \"~6\"\n340\t          },\n341\t          {\n342\t            \"stage\": \"GRPO final frac_zero_std\",\n343\t            \"rasp_25\": \"0.98\",\n344\t            \"standard_25\": \"0.96\"\n345\t          }\n346\t        ]\n347\t      },\n348\t      {\n349\t        \"name\": \"Table: Collapse gradient comparison across sparsity\",\n350\t        \"rows\": [\n351\t          {\n352\t            \"sparsity\": \"20%\",\n353\t            \"rasp_collapse\": \"step 10\",\n354\t            \"standard_collapse\": \"step 60\",\n355\t            \"ratio\": \"6.0x\"\n356\t          },\n357\t          {\n358\t            \"sparsity\": \"25%\",\n359\t            \"rasp_collapse\": \"step 4\",\n360\t            \"standard_collapse\": \"step 6\",\n361\t            \"ratio\": \"1.5x\"\n362\t          }\n363\t        ]\n364\t      }\n365\t    ],\n366\t    \"figures\": [],\n367\t    \"analysis\": \"25% sparsity完全消解了collapse severity gradient。两者都太脆弱无法sustain GRPO training。Reviewer会argue: '你的diagnostic只在一个sparsity点work(20%)，换个sparsity就break——这不是robust mechanism而是coincidence。' SFT gap也shrink到不显著(0.75pp, p=0.35)。Worst档核心结论：Redundancy-Stability Tradeoff在25%下不可观测。\\n\\n25%是worst档的critical sparsity。Post-prune: RASP 21% vs Standard 16%（已confirmed）。Post-SFT: RASP ~52% vs Standard ~51.25%（已有Standard数据），gap缩小到<1pp (p=0.35)——因为higher sparsity下SFT recovery能力更受限于absolute damage而非which structures were removed。GRPO: 关键——两者都在≤10步内collapse。RASP step 4, Standard step 6，ratio仅0.67（不是20%下的6x差距）。这是因为25% sparsity下两个模型的exploration capacity都已被破坏到临界值以下，collapse变成near-deterministic而非structure-dependent。Severity gradient消失——无法区分'redundancy removal causing fast collapse' vs 'general over-pruning causing universal collapse'。\"\n368\t  },\n369\t  {\n370\t    \"name\": \"30% Sparsity Probe\",\n371\t    \"description\": \"30% sparsity prune + eval only (no recovery) for RASP and Standard\",\n372\t    \"results\": {\n373\t      \"rasp_30_post_prune_accuracy\": 0.08,\n374\t      \"standard_30_post_prune_accuracy\": 0.06,\n375\t      \"rasp_30_eos_rate\": 0.25,\n376\t      \"standard_30_eos_rate\": 0.18,\n377\t      \"gap_pp\": 2.0,\n378\t      \"p_value\": 0.55\n379\t    },\n380\t    \"tables\": [\n381\t      {\n382\t        \"name\": \"Table: 30% sparsity post-prune\",\n383\t        \"rows\": [\n384\t          {\n385\t            \"method\": \"RASP-30%\",\n386\t            \"accuracy\": \"8%\",\n387\t            \"eos_rate\": \"25%\",\n388\t            \"avg_len\": \"3200\"\n389\t          },\n390\t          {\n391\t            \"method\": \"Standard-30%\",\n392\t            \"accuracy\": \"6%\",\n393\t            \"eos_rate\": \"18%\",\n394\t            \"avg_len\": \"3500\"\n395\t          }\n396\t        ]\n397\t      }\n398\t    ],\n399\t    \"figures\": [],\n400\t    \"analysis\": \"Confirms sparsity ceiling但对method comparison无价值。在worst档下用作evidence that structured pruning has narrow useful range (practical limitation)。\\n\\n30% sparsity下两者都接近complete collapse (8% vs 6%)。Model基本无法生成coherent reasoning。Gap 2pp在这个regime下meaningless——两者都是catastrophically damaged。这confirms 25-30%是DeepSeek-R1-Distill-Qwen-7B structured pruning的hard ceiling，但不提供任何method-differentiating evidence。\"\n401\t  },\n402\t  {\n403\t    \"name\": \"Extended Evaluation (MMLU, HumanEval, MATH-500)\",\n404\t    \"description\": \"Best recovered config on OOD benchmarks\",\n405\t    \"results\": {\n406\t      \"rasp_20_sft_mmlu\": 0.48,\n407\t      \"rasp_20_sft_humaneval\": 0.35,\n408\t      \"rasp_20_sft_math500\": 0.28,\n409\t      \"standard_20_sft_mmlu\": 0.47,\n410\t      \"standard_20_sft_humaneval\": 0.33,\n411\t      \"standard_20_sft_math500\": 0.26,\n412\t      \"unpruned_sft_mmlu\": 0.62,\n413\t      \"unpruned_sft_humaneval\": 0.55,\n414\t      \"unpruned_sft_math500\": 0.52,\n415\t      \"rasp_vs_standard_mmlu_p\": 0.62,\n416\t      \"rasp_vs_standard_humaneval_p\": 0.45,\n417\t      \"rasp_vs_standard_math500_p\": 0.38\n418\t    },\n419\t    \"tables\": [\n420\t      {\n421\t        \"name\": \"Table: Extended evaluation\",\n422\t        \"rows\": [\n423\t          {\n424\t            \"benchmark\": \"MMLU\",\n425\t            \"unpruned\": \"62%\",\n426\t            \"rasp_20\": \"48%\",\n427\t            \"standard_20\": \"47%\",\n428\t            \"gap_pp\": \"+1pp\",\n429\t            \"p\": \"0.62\"\n430\t          },\n431\t          {\n432\t            \"benchmark\": \"HumanEval\",\n433\t            \"unpruned\": \"55%\",\n434\t            \"rasp_20\": \"35%\",\n435\t            \"standard_20\": \"33%\",\n436\t            \"gap_pp\": \"+2pp\",\n437\t            \"p\": \"0.45\"\n438\t          },\n439\t          {\n440\t            \"benchmark\": \"MATH-500\",\n441\t            \"unpruned\": \"52%\",\n442\t            \"rasp_20\": \"28%\",\n443\t            \"standard_20\": \"26%\",\n444\t            \"gap_pp\": \"+2pp\",\n445\t            \"p\": \"0.38\"\n446\t          }\n447\t        ]\n448\t      }\n449\t    ],\n450\t    \"figures\": [],\n451\t    \"analysis\": \"RASP advantage不generalize beyond GSM8K。在worst档下这是expected——如果GSM8K上gap都不显著，OOD上更不可能significant。但pruned models的uniform degradation strengthens 'structured pruning is destructive' narrative。\\n\\nOOD benchmarks下RASP vs Standard gap同样不显著。MMLU差1pp, HumanEval差2pp, MATH差2pp——都在noise range内。这是因为SFT recovery是domain-agnostic的(teacher-forcing on GSM8K)，CKA-aware pruning的marginal structural advantage不transfer到其他tasks。Worst档下这进一步confirms RASP无meaningful advantage。同时，pruned vs unpruned的大幅drop (MATH: 52%→27%)表明structured pruning造成的reasoning能力损失是across-domain的。\"\n452\t  },\n453\t  {\n454\t    \"name\": \"Bonsai Baseline 20%\",\n455\t    \"description\": \"Bonsai (ICML 2025) gradient-free structured pruning at 20% sparsity\",\n456\t    \"results\": {\n457\t      \"bonsai_post_prune_accuracy\": 0.24,\n458\t      \"bonsai_post_sft_accuracy\": 0.56,\n459\t      \"bonsai_post_grpo_collapse_step\": 8,\n460\t      \"bonsai_grpo_peak_reward\": 0.019,\n461\t      \"bonsai_grpo_final_frac_zero_std\": 0.93\n462\t    },\n463\t    \"tables\": [\n464\t      {\n465\t        \"name\": \"Table: Method comparison including Bonsai\",\n466\t        \"rows\": [\n467\t          {\n468\t            \"method\": \"RASP\",\n469\t            \"post_prune\": \"31%\",\n470\t            \"post_sft\": \"61.5%\",\n471\t            \"grpo_collapse\": \"step 10\"\n472\t          },\n473\t          {\n474\t            \"method\": \"Standard\",\n475\t            \"post_prune\": \"27%\",\n476\t            \"post_sft\": \"59.3%\",\n477\t            \"grpo_collapse\": \"step 60\"\n478\t          },\n479\t          {\n480\t            \"method\": \"Bonsai\",\n481\t            \"post_prune\": \"24%\",\n482\t            \"post_sft\": \"56%\",\n483\t            \"grpo_collapse\": \"step 8\"\n484\t          },\n485\t          {\n486\t            \"method\": \"GRASPrune\",\n487\t            \"post_prune\": \"7%\",\n488\t            \"post_sft\": \"41%\",\n489\t            \"grpo_collapse\": \"step 5\"\n490\t          }\n491\t        ]\n492\t      }\n493\t    ],\n494\t    \"figures\": [],\n495\t    \"analysis\": \"Bonsai数据reveals collapse speed几乎perfectly correlates with post-SFT accuracy (r≈0.95)。Worst档下reviewer会argue: 'RASP collapses fast不是因为它removed redundancy, 而是因为它happens to produce slightly lower SFT quality than Standard (61.5 vs 59.3, but at 25% the gap disappears and so does the collapse difference)。Collapse is trivially predicted by model quality, not by structural damage type。'\\n\\nBonsai是gradient-free方法，通常在structured pruning中accuracy略低于gradient-based方法。Post-prune 24% (between random 18% and Standard 27%)。Post-SFT recovery到56%——低于RASP(61.5%)和Standard(59.3%)但仍reasonable。GRPO collapse at step 8——和RASP(step 10)同量级。在worst档下，Bonsai的加入进一步demonstrates所有structured pruning的GRPO都collapse，且collapse speed和post-SFT quality正相关（trivialy: worse model = faster collapse）。不提供redundancy-specific insight。\"\n496\t  },\n497\t  {\n498\t    \"name\": \"CKA Reliability Analysis\",\n499\t    \"description\": \"Split-half consistency + calibration size sensitivity\",\n500\t    \"results\": {\n501\t      \"split_half_spearman_rho\": 0.72,\n502\t      \"cal_256_vs_512_rank_corr\": 0.78,\n503\t      \"cal_512_vs_1024_rank_corr\": 0.85,\n504\t      \"score_variance_across_splits\": 0.15,\n505\t      \"top_20pct_overlap_across_splits\": 0.68\n506\t    },\n507\t    \"tables\": [\n508\t      {\n509\t        \"name\": \"Table: CKA reliability metrics\",\n510\t        \"rows\": [\n511\t          {\n512\t            \"metric\": \"Split-half Spearman ρ\",\n513\t            \"value\": \"0.72\"\n514\t          },\n515\t          {\n516\t            \"metric\": \"Cal-256 vs Cal-512 rank corr\",\n517\t            \"value\": \"0.78\"\n518\t          },\n519\t          {\n520\t            \"metric\": \"Cal-512 vs Cal-1024 rank corr\",\n521\t            \"value\": \"0.85\"\n522\t          },\n523\t          {\n524\t            \"metric\": \"Top-20% set overlap (split-half)\",\n525\t            \"value\": \"68%\"\n526\t          }\n527\t        ]\n528\t      }\n529\t    ],\n530\t    \"figures\": [],\n531\t    \"analysis\": \"CKA reliability是acceptable but not high。32% decision instability在worst档下被interpret为：RASP的marginal advantage可能just是particular calibration sample的artifact而非stable structural property。\\n\\nCKA scores本身有moderate reliability (ρ=0.72 split-half)，不算terrible但也不够high for confident structure selection。Top-20% pruned structures只有68% overlap across splits——意味着32%的pruning decisions是unstable的。Calibration size从256→512→1024确实improves (0.78→0.85)，但512 (我们用的) 仍有notable instability。Worst档下这undermines RASP scoring的reliability——如果CKA scores themselves are noisy，基于它们的pruning decision也是noisy的。\"\n532\t  },\n533\t  {\n534\t    \"name\": \"Alpha Sensitivity Ablation\",\n535\t    \"description\": \"α ∈ {0, 0.25, 0.5, 1, 2} sweep in RASP scoring at 20% sparsity, post-prune + post-SFT eval\",\n536\t    \"results\": {\n537\t      \"alpha_0_post_prune\": 0.27,\n538\t      \"alpha_0_post_sft\": 0.64,\n539\t      \"alpha_0p25_post_prune\": 0.23,\n540\t      \"alpha_0p25_post_sft\": 0.58,\n541\t      \"alpha_0p5_post_prune\": 0.22,\n542\t      \"alpha_0p5_post_sft\": 0.55,\n543\t      \"alpha_1p0_post_prune\": 0.31,\n544\t      \"alpha_1p0_post_sft\": 0.57,\n545\t      \"alpha_2p0_post_prune\": 0.36,\n546\t      \"alpha_2p0_post_sft\": 0.62,\n547\t      \"optimal_alpha_post_prune\": 2.0,\n548\t      \"optimal_alpha_post_sft\": 0.0,\n549\t      \"correlation_postprune_vs_postsft\": -0.45\n550\t    },\n551\t    \"tables\": [\n552\t      {\n553\t        \"name\": \"Table: Alpha ablation full pipeline\",\n554\t        \"rows\": [\n555\t          {\n556\t            \"alpha\": \"0.0 (=Standard)\",\n557\t            \"post_prune\": \"27%\",\n558\t            \"post_sft\": \"64%\",\n559\t            \"post_sft_ci\": \"±4.7%\"\n560\t          },\n561\t          {\n562\t            \"alpha\": \"0.25\",\n563\t            \"post_prune\": \"23%\",\n564\t            \"post_sft\": \"58%\",\n565\t            \"post_sft_ci\": \"±4.9%\"\n566\t          },\n567\t          {\n568\t            \"alpha\": \"0.5\",\n569\t            \"post_prune\": \"22%\",\n570\t            \"post_sft\": \"55%\",\n571\t            \"post_sft_ci\": \"±5.0%\"\n572\t          },\n573\t          {\n574\t            \"alpha\": \"1.0 (=RASP)\",\n575\t            \"post_prune\": \"31%\",\n576\t            \"post_sft\": \"57%\",\n577\t            \"post_sft_ci\": \"±5.0%\"\n578\t          },\n579\t          {\n580\t            \"alpha\": \"2.0\",\n581\t            \"post_prune\": \"36%\",\n582\t            \"post_sft\": \"62%\",\n583\t            \"post_sft_ci\": \"±4.9%\"\n584\t          }\n585\t        ]\n586\t      }\n587\t    ],\n588\t    \"figures\": [],\n589\t    \"analysis\": \"α ablation是worst档最damaging的实验。Post-prune accuracy和post-SFT accuracy decouple——CKA optimization of post-prune is a wrong objective。α=0 (no CKA, Standard) achieves highest post-SFT despite lowest post-prune。RASP's core insight ('remove redundant structures because they're safely recoverable') is empirically falsified: recovering redundant-structure-preserving models is NOT easier。\\n\\n已有post-prune数据(α=0:27%, α=0.25:23%, α=0.5:22%, α=1:31%, α=2:36%)。Post-SFT数据在worst档下shows反转：α=0(即Standard，无CKA)给出最高post-SFT(64%)，而α=2(强CKA weighting, 最高post-prune)给出62%。α和post-SFT accuracy无单调关系，且post-prune和post-SFT accuracy negatively correlated (r=-0.45)——高post-prune不predict高post-SFT。这is devastating: RASP的CKA modulation optimizes wrong proxy。保留high-CKA structures helps immediate post-prune accuracy但doesn't help (甚至slightly hurts) SFT recovery。\"\n590\t  },\n591\t  {\n592\t    \"name\": \"Inference Speedup Benchmark\",\n593\t    \"description\": \"Wall-clock latency + throughput for dense vs 20% RASP vs 20% Standard\",\n594\t    \"results\": {\n595\t      \"dense_latency_ms_per_token\": 18.5,\n596\t      \"rasp_20_latency_ms_per_token\": 16.2,\n597\t      \"standard_20_latency_ms_per_token\": 16.0,\n598\t      \"dense_throughput_tokens_per_sec\": 54.1,\n599\t      \"rasp_20_throughput_tokens_per_sec\": 61.7,\n600\t      \"standard_20_throughput_tokens_per_sec\": 62.5,\n601\t      \"speedup_rasp_vs_dense\": 1.14,\n602\t      \"speedup_standard_vs_dense\": 1.16,\n603\t      \"memory_reduction_pct\": 18.5\n604\t    },\n605\t    \"tables\": [\n606\t      {\n607\t        \"name\": \"Table: Inference efficiency\",\n608\t        \"rows\": [\n609\t          {\n610\t            \"model\": \"Dense (7.6B)\",\n611\t            \"latency_ms\": \"18.5\",\n612\t            \"throughput\": \"54.1 tok/s\",\n613\t            \"memory_gb\": \"15.2\"\n614\t          },\n615\t          {\n616\t            \"model\": \"RASP-20% (6.2B)\",\n617\t            \"latency_ms\": \"16.2\",\n618\t            \"throughput\": \"61.7 tok/s\",\n619\t            \"memory_gb\": \"12.4\"\n620\t          },\n621\t          {\n622\t            \"model\": \"Standard-20% (6.2B)\",\n623\t            \"latency_ms\": \"16.0\",\n624\t            \"throughput\": \"62.5 tok/s\",\n625\t            \"memory_gb\": \"12.4\"\n626\t          }\n627\t        ]\n628\t      }\n629\t    ],\n630\t    \"figures\": [],\n631\t    \"analysis\": \"Inference speedup insufficient to justify accuracy cost。Worst档下这weaken practical motivation：如果structured pruning只给14% speedup with 25% accuracy loss，research question本身的relevance被questioned。需要在paper中reframe为'studying fundamental interaction'而非'practical compression method'。\\n\\n20% structured pruning只给14-16% speedup。这是因为：(1) MLP-only pruning (attn groups未被pruned) 限制了speedup ceiling; (2) GPU利用率在batch_size=1时不是memory-bound; (3) Structured pruning的实际speedup远低于theoretical FLOP reduction (20%)因为kernel launch overhead和memory bandwidth不是线性关系。Worst档下1.14-1.16x speedup is disappointing——不足以justify 20pp+ accuracy loss (81%→61%)。Reviewer: 'you lose 20pp accuracy for 14% speedup — no practitioner would make this trade。'\"\n632\t  },\n633\t  {\n634\t    \"name\": \"Unstructured Pruning Baseline 20%\",\n635\t    \"description\": \"Magnitude-based unstructured pruning at 20%, eval + SFT → GRPO\",\n636\t    \"results\": {\n637\t      \"unstructured_20_post_prune_accuracy\": 0.72,\n638\t      \"unstructured_20_post_sft_accuracy\": 0.79,\n639\t      \"unstructured_20_grpo_accuracy\": 0.79,\n640\t      \"unstructured_20_grpo_collapse\": false,\n641\t      \"unstructured_20_grpo_steps_stable\": 100,\n642\t      \"unstructured_20_grpo_final_reward\": 0.55\n643\t    },\n644\t    \"tables\": [\n645\t      {\n646\t        \"name\": \"Table: Structured vs Unstructured comparison\",\n647\t        \"rows\": [\n648\t          {\n649\t            \"method\": \"Dense\",\n650\t            \"post_prune\": \"81%\",\n651\t            \"post_sft\": \"81%\",\n652\t            \"grpo_collapse\": \"No\",\n653\t            \"grpo_accuracy\": \"81%\"\n654\t          },\n655\t          {\n656\t            \"method\": \"Unstructured-20%\",\n657\t            \"post_prune\": \"72%\",\n658\t            \"post_sft\": \"79%\",\n659\t            \"grpo_collapse\": \"No\",\n660\t            \"grpo_accuracy\": \"79%\"\n661\t          },\n662\t          {\n663\t            \"method\": \"RASP-Structured-20%\",\n664\t            \"post_prune\": \"31%\",\n665\t            \"post_sft\": \"61.5%\",\n666\t            \"grpo_collapse\": \"Step 10\",\n667\t            \"grpo_accuracy\": \"60.7%\"\n668\t          },\n669\t          {\n670\t            \"method\": \"Standard-Structured-20%\",\n671\t            \"post_prune\": \"27%\",\n672\t            \"post_sft\": \"59.3%\",\n673\t            \"grpo_collapse\": \"Step 60\",\n674\t            \"grpo_accuracy\": \"58.9%\"\n675\t          }\n676\t        ]\n677\t      }\n678\t    ],\n679\t    \"figures\": [],\n680\t    \"analysis\": \"Unstructured doesn't collapse → GRPO failure是structured-pruning-specific。Worst档下reviewer会reframe为capacity argument: 'structured pruning removes 20% of architecture but >>20% of effective capacity (因为removes entire functional units)，collapse是trivially因为model太弱not因为any specific structural property'。这undermines Redundancy-Stability Tradeoff的mechanistic claim进一步。\\n\\nUnstructured pruning at 20% preserves大部分accuracy (72% post-prune vs structured 27-31%)因为individual weight zeroing比removing entire structures damage far less。Post-SFT recovery到79%接近dense baseline (81%)。关键：GRPO在unstructured pruned model上NOT collapse——100 steps stable, reward reaches 0.55。这directly refutes 'pruning breaks RLVR'的general claim，narrowing it to'STRUCTURED pruning breaks RLVR'。In worst档: 这是double-edged。一方面narrows scope (only structured matters)；另一方面reviewer可能argue 'if unstructured doesn't collapse, your finding is about model capacity, not redundancy — 20% structured removes much more effective capacity than 20% unstructured'。\"\n681\t  },\n682\t  {\n683\t    \"name\": \"SFT OOD Eval Contingency\",\n684\t    \"description\": \"Standard SFT-recovered model (64%→59.3% GSM8K) on MATH-500 and HumanEval\",\n685\t    \"results\": {\n686\t      \"standard_sft_math500\": 0.22,\n687\t      \"standard_sft_humaneval\": 0.28,\n688\t      \"rasp_sft_math500\": 0.24,\n689\t      \"rasp_sft_humaneval\": 0.3,\n690\t      \"unpruned_sft_math500\": 0.52,\n691\t      \"unpruned_sft_humaneval\": 0.55,\n692\t      \"gap_math500_pp\": 2.0,\n693\t      \"gap_humaneval_pp\": 2.0,\n694\t      \"gap_math500_p\": 0.35,\n695\t      \"gap_humaneval_p\": 0.4\n696\t    },\n697\t    \"tables\": [\n698\t      {\n699\t        \"name\": \"Table: OOD evaluation\",\n700\t        \"rows\": [\n701\t          {\n702\t            \"benchmark\": \"MATH-500\",\n703\t            \"unpruned\": \"52%\",\n704\t            \"rasp_20\": \"24%\",\n705\t            \"standard_20\": \"22%\",\n706\t            \"p_value\": \"0.35\"\n707\t          },\n708\t          {\n709\t            \"benchmark\": \"HumanEval\",\n710\t            \"unpruned\": \"55%\",\n711\t            \"rasp_20\": \"30%\",\n712\t            \"standard_20\": \"28%\",\n713\t            \"p_value\": \"0.40\"\n714\t          },\n715\t          {\n716\t            \"benchmark\": \"GSM8K\",\n717\t            \"unpruned\": \"81%\",\n718\t            \"rasp_20\": \"61.5%\",\n719\t            \"standard_20\": \"59.3%\",\n720\t            \"p_value\": \"0.25\"\n721\t          }\n722\t        ]\n723\t      }\n724\t    ],\n725\t    \"figures\": [],\n726\t    \"analysis\": \"OOD collapse suggests SFT recovery是GSM8K-specific memorization。Worst档下这weakens 'SFT-only recovery as practical recommendation'——如果SFT只恢复in-domain performance，recommendation的practical scope极其有限。\\n\\nOOD evaluation下RASP vs Standard gap同样tiny (2pp, p>0.35)。两个pruned models在harder benchmarks上都heavily degraded vs unpruned (MATH: 22-24% vs 52%, HumanEval: 28-30% vs 55%)。这表明SFT recovery在GSM8K-domain外效果很差——recovery是domain-specific pattern memorization而非genuine reasoning restoration。Worst档下这进一步削弱SFT recovery作为practical solution的framing，但不directly影响GRPO failure narrative。\"\n727\t  },\n728\t  {\n729\t    \"name\": \"Qwen-Math-7B RASP/Standard 20% SFT Eval\",\n730\t    \"description\": \"Qwen2.5-Math-7B pruned at 20% (RASP + Standard), SFT recovery, N=200 eval\",\n731\t    \"results\": {\n732\t      \"rasp_20_qwen_sft_accuracy\": 0.725,\n733\t      \"standard_20_qwen_sft_accuracy\": 0.71,\n734\t      \"gap_pp\": 1.5,\n735\t      \"gap_p_value\": 0.42\n736\t    },\n737\t    \"tables\": [\n738\t      {\n739\t        \"name\": \"Table: Cross-model 20% SFT\",\n740\t        \"rows\": [\n741\t          {\n742\t            \"model\": \"DeepSeek-R1-Distill-Qwen-7B\",\n743\t            \"rasp\": \"61.5%\",\n744\t            \"standard\": \"59.3%\",\n745\t            \"gap\": \"+2.2pp\"\n746\t          },\n747\t          {\n748\t            \"model\": \"Qwen2.5-Math-7B\",\n749\t            \"rasp\": \"72.5%\",\n750\t            \"standard\": \"71.0%\",\n751\t            \"gap\": \"+1.5pp\"\n752\t          }\n753\t        ]\n754\t      }\n755\t    ],\n756\t    \"figures\": [],\n757\t    \"analysis\": \"Cross-model SFT gap even smaller。RASP advantage不robust across models。\\n\\n已有实验数据: RASP 72.5% vs Standard 71%。Gap仅1.5pp (p=0.42)——比DeepSeek-R1上的2.2pp还小。Cross-model下CKA-aware pruning的advantage进一步diminish，因为Qwen-Math的architecture redundancy pattern可能不同于DeepSeek-R1-Distill。\"\n758\t  },\n759\t  {\n760\t    \"name\": \"Qwen-Math-7B RASP/Standard 25% Full Pipeline\",\n761\t    \"description\": \"Qwen2.5-Math-7B pruned at 25% (RASP + Standard), SFT + GRPO, N=200 eval\",\n762\t    \"results\": {\n763\t      \"rasp_25_qwen_sft_accuracy\": 0.64,\n764\t      \"standard_25_qwen_sft_accuracy\": 0.63,\n765\t      \"sft_gap_pp\": 1.0,\n766\t      \"sft_gap_p_value\": 0.48,\n767\t      \"grpo_rasp_25_qwen_collapse_step\": 7,\n768\t      \"grpo_standard_25_qwen_collapse_step\": 8,\n769\t      \"grpo_rasp_25_qwen_peak_reward\": 0.022,\n770\t      \"grpo_standard_25_qwen_peak_reward\": 0.025,\n771\t      \"collapse_ratio\": 0.875\n772\t    },\n773\t    \"tables\": [\n774\t      {\n775\t        \"name\": \"Table: Qwen-Math 25% GRPO collapse comparison\",\n776\t        \"rows\": [\n777\t          {\n778\t            \"model\": \"DeepSeek-R1 25%\",\n779\t            \"rasp_collapse\": \"step 4\",\n780\t            \"standard_collapse\": \"step 6\",\n781\t            \"ratio\": \"1.5x\"\n782\t          },\n783\t          {\n784\t            \"model\": \"Qwen-Math 25%\",\n785\t            \"rasp_collapse\": \"step 7\",\n786\t            \"standard_collapse\": \"step 8\",\n787\t            \"ratio\": \"1.14x\"\n788\t          },\n789\t          {\n790\t            \"model\": \"DeepSeek-R1 20%\",\n791\t            \"rasp_collapse\": \"step 10\",\n792\t            \"standard_collapse\": \"step 60\",\n793\t            \"ratio\": \"6.0x\"\n794\t          },\n795\t          {\n796\t            \"model\": \"Qwen-Math 20%\",\n797\t            \"rasp_collapse\": \"TBD\",\n798\t            \"standard_collapse\": \"TBD\",\n799\t            \"ratio\": \"TBD\"\n800\t          }\n801\t        ]\n802\t      }\n803\t    ],\n804\t    \"figures\": [],\n805\t    \"analysis\": \"Cross-model non-reproducibility是worst档的killshot for mechanism claim。如果collapse gradient只在one model × one sparsity下observe，它不是generalizable mechanism而是coincidence。\\n\\nWorst档核心: Qwen-Math上GRPO collapse差异消失。RASP step 7 vs Standard step 8——ratio 0.875 (within noise)。两者都rapidly collapse，无severity gradient。这directly falsifies 'collapse speed diagnoses structural damage type' claim跨模型。原因：Qwen-Math的internal redundancy structure可能不同(more uniform, less exploitable by CKA)，或25% sparsity对Qwen-Math已经是critical threshold (Qwen-Math baseline更高所以25% damage也更severe in relative terms)。\"\n806\t  }\n807\t]"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"382d3fca-c918-4d79-9064-e8f82775e1fe","uuid":"d0abff1c-3ae9-417b-a419-75107a7bac1a","timestamp":"2026-05-16T15:24:39.362Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_17/projects/recovery_aware_struct_prune/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260516T144805/worst/experiment_data.json","content":"[\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Full GSM8K Eval Baseline + RASP_20 + Standard_20\",\n    \"description\": \"Full test set (N=1319) eval for all three conditions at 20% sparsity\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"unpruned_accuracy\": 0.8127,\n      \"rasp_20_post_prune_accuracy\": 0.31,\n      \"standard_20_post_prune_accuracy\": 0.27,\n      \"rasp_vs_standard_gap_pp\": 4.0,\n      \"rasp_vs_standard_p_value\": 0.38,\n      \"ci_width_pp\": 2.5\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: Post-prune accuracy (N=1319)\",\n        \"rows\": [\n          {\n            \"method\": \"Unpruned\",\n            \"accuracy\": \"81.27%\",\n            \"stderr\": \"±1.07pp\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"method\": \"RASP-20%\",\n            \"accuracy\": \"30.5%\",\n            \"stderr\": \"±2.54pp\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"method\": \"Standard-20%\",\n            \"accuracy\": \"27.1%\",\n            \"stderr\": \"±2.45pp\"\n          }\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Post-prune gap不显著，不能claim RASP preserves more reasoning capacity pre-recovery。两者都严重degraded到接近random baseline (GSM8K ≈ 0% for truly random)。\\n\\n已有N=100数据(RASP 31% vs Standard 27%)在full eval下只能微幅收敛。4pp gap在N=1319下仍不显著(p≈0.38)，因为post-prune accuracy本身variance大、两者都在random-ish低准确率区间。Worst档下这个gap不构成meaningful difference。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Full GSM8K Eval All Recovered Models\",\n    \"description\": \"N=1319 eval for SFT-recovered and GRPO-recovered models (RASP_20, Standard_20, unpruned)\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"sft_rasp_20_accuracy\": 0.6149,\n      \"sft_standard_20_accuracy\": 0.5929,\n      \"sft_gap_20_pp\": 2.2,\n      \"sft_gap_20_p_value\": 0.25,\n      \"grpo_rasp_step5_accuracy\": 0.6065,\n      \"grpo_standard_step50_accuracy\": 0.5891,\n      \"grpo_unpruned_step100_accuracy\": 0.8127,\n      \"grpo_unpruned_delta_vs_sft\": 0.0\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table 1: Recovery accuracy comparison (N=1319)\",\n        \"rows\": [\n          {\n            \"condition\": \"Unpruned SFT\",\n            \"accuracy\": \"81.27%\",\n            \"grpo_accuracy\": \"81.27%\",\n            \"delta\": \"0.00pp\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"condition\": \"RASP-20% SFT\",\n            \"accuracy\": \"61.49%\",\n            \"grpo_accuracy\": \"60.65%\",\n            \"delta\": \"-0.84pp\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"condition\": \"Standard-20% SFT\",\n            \"accuracy\": \"59.29%\",\n            \"grpo_accuracy\": \"58.91%\",\n            \"delta\": \"-0.38pp\"\n          }\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Universal reward-accuracy decoupling confirmed。但SFT gap (RASP vs Standard) 在p=0.25下insufficient to support Redundancy-Stability Tradeoff claim。论文只能claim GRPO failure是universal，而非pruning-method-specific。\\n\\n这些数据已实际收集完毕。SFT gap 2.2pp (p=0.25)在worst档下被视为不显著。GRPO对所有模型都不提升accuracy（unpruned: 0.00pp, Standard: -0.38pp, RASP: -0.84pp），这是strong negative result但不需要RASP-specific解释。Collapse dynamics差异（RASP step10 vs Standard step60）在20%下存在，但worst档的核心问题是这个gradient在25%下消失。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"GRASPrune Baseline 20% Sparsity\",\n    \"description\": \"GRASPrune (ACL 2026 SOTA) at 20% sparsity: prune → eval → SFT → GRPO full pipeline\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"grasp_post_prune_accuracy\": 0.07,\n      \"grasp_post_sft_accuracy\": 0.41,\n      \"grasp_post_grpo_step30_accuracy\": 0.39,\n      \"grasp_grpo_collapse_step\": 5,\n      \"grasp_grpo_final_reward\": 0.012,\n      \"grasp_grpo_frac_zero_std_final\": 0.97\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: GRASPrune pipeline comparison\",\n        \"rows\": [\n          {\n            \"stage\": \"Post-prune\",\n            \"grasp\": \"7%\",\n            \"rasp\": \"31%\",\n            \"standard\": \"27%\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"stage\": \"Post-SFT\",\n            \"grasp\": \"41%\",\n            \"rasp\": \"61.5%\",\n            \"standard\": \"59.3%\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"stage\": \"Post-GRPO\",\n            \"grasp\": \"39%\",\n            \"rasp\": \"60.7%\",\n            \"standard\": \"58.9%\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"stage\": \"GRPO collapse step\",\n            \"grasp\": \"~5\",\n            \"rasp\": \"~10\",\n            \"standard\": \"~60\"\n          }\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"GRASPrune数据confirms所有structured pruning methods的GRPO都fail，但severity ordering (GRASPrune < RASP < Standard)在worst档下被解释为trivially correlated with post-SFT quality而非redundancy-specific mechanism。Reviewer会argue: 'collapse speed simply tracks model quality, not structural damage type'。\\n\\nGRASPrune在post-prune (7%)和post-SFT (41%)都远低于RASP(31%→61%)和Standard(27%→59%)。这是因为GRASPrune的gate-based selection在reasoning model上suboptimal——它优化一般loss而非reasoning trace。在worst档下，GRASPrune GRPO会比RASP更快collapse(step 5)，但这不提供diagnostic value因为GRASPrune本身就是inferior pruning，collapse快是trivial结论。这个baseline反而削弱了RASP的novelty——如果所有结构化剪枝方法的GRPO都collapse，那collapse不是RASP-specific insight。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Multi-seed Post-prune Eval\",\n    \"description\": \"5 seeds (incl. seed 42) for RASP_20 + Standard_20 post-prune eval, variance estimation\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"rasp_20_mean_accuracy\": 0.305,\n      \"rasp_20_std\": 0.018,\n      \"standard_20_mean_accuracy\": 0.278,\n      \"standard_20_std\": 0.022,\n      \"mean_gap_pp\": 2.7,\n      \"paired_t_p_value\": 0.15,\n      \"cohens_d\": 0.42\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: Multi-seed post-prune accuracy\",\n        \"rows\": [\n          {\n            \"seed\": 42,\n            \"rasp\": \"31%\",\n            \"standard\": \"27%\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"seed\": 123,\n            \"rasp\": \"29%\",\n            \"standard\": \"28%\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"seed\": 456,\n            \"rasp\": \"32%\",\n            \"standard\": \"30%\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"seed\": 789,\n            \"rasp\": \"28%\",\n            \"standard\": \"26%\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"seed\": 1024,\n            \"rasp\": \"32.5%\",\n            \"standard\": \"28%\"\n          }\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Multi-seed证据weak。Gap存在但不robust (p=0.15)。在worst档下这strengthens the narrative that CKA-aware scoring的marginal benefit不justify方法复杂度。\\n\\nPost-prune accuracy受calibration sample variance影响。5 seeds下RASP mean ≈ 30.5%, Standard mean ≈ 27.8%, gap ~2.7pp。但std较大(1.8-2.2pp)导致paired-t test p≈0.15。Worst档下reviewers会argue这个gap不足以支持CKA-aware scoring的优越性。Cohen's d=0.42 (medium effect)不够convincing for a core method claim。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Scoring Ablation (magnitude/gradient/random)\",\n    \"description\": \"Ablation: magnitude-only, gradient-only, random pruning at 20% sparsity\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"magnitude_only_accuracy\": 0.26,\n      \"gradient_only_accuracy\": 0.29,\n      \"random_pruning_accuracy\": 0.18,\n      \"rasp_accuracy_ref\": 0.31,\n      \"standard_accuracy_ref\": 0.27,\n      \"gradient_vs_rasp_gap\": 2.0,\n      \"gradient_vs_rasp_p_value\": 0.41\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: Scoring method ablation (20% sparsity, N=100)\",\n        \"rows\": [\n          {\n            \"method\": \"RASP (I×(1-F)^α)\",\n            \"accuracy\": \"31%\",\n            \"stderr\": \"±4.6%\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"method\": \"Gradient-only (I)\",\n            \"accuracy\": \"29%\",\n            \"stderr\": \"±4.5%\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"method\": \"Standard (importance)\",\n            \"accuracy\": \"27%\",\n            \"stderr\": \"±4.4%\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"method\": \"Magnitude-only\",\n            \"accuracy\": \"26%\",\n            \"stderr\": \"±4.4%\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"method\": \"Random\",\n            \"accuracy\": \"18%\",\n            \"stderr\": \"±3.8%\"\n          }\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"CKA modulation的贡献被noise淹没。Worst档叙事：RASP's CKA component is at best marginal (2pp over gradient-only, p=0.41)。不足以支持CKA作为method contribution。\\n\\nWorst档下，gradient-only(即Standard的核心——importance scoring)已达到29%，接近RASP的31%。CKA modulation仅额外贡献~2pp，这在N=100下完全不显著(p=0.41)。Magnitude-only(26%)和Standard(27%)几乎相同，说明importance metric差异在post-prune这个极低accuracy regime下noise-dominated。Random(18%)是唯一clearly worse的，但这是trivial——任何informed method都应该beat random。Ablation结果undermine CKA的独立贡献。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Per-structure CKA-Recoverability Correlation\",\n    \"description\": \"Per-head F(h) vs activation change after recovery, mixed-effects regression\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"pearson_r_fh_vs_activation_change\": 0.12,\n      \"spearman_rho\": 0.09,\n      \"mixed_effects_p_value_fh\": 0.31,\n      \"variance_explained_by_fh\": 0.014,\n      \"weight_norm_variance_explained\": 0.08,\n      \"gradient_importance_variance_explained\": 0.11\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: Mixed-effects regression coefficients\",\n        \"rows\": [\n          {\n            \"predictor\": \"F(h) (CKA redundancy)\",\n            \"beta\": \"0.034\",\n            \"p_value\": \"0.31\",\n            \"R²_partial\": \"0.014\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"predictor\": \"Weight norm\",\n            \"beta\": \"0.089\",\n            \"p_value\": \"0.02\",\n            \"R²_partial\": \"0.08\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"predictor\": \"Gradient importance\",\n            \"beta\": \"0.102\",\n            \"p_value\": \"0.008\",\n            \"R²_partial\": \"0.11\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"predictor\": \"Activation magnitude\",\n            \"beta\": \"0.076\",\n            \"p_value\": \"0.04\",\n            \"R²_partial\": \"0.06\"\n          }\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"CKA-based redundancy metric不predict recovery behavior。在worst档下这是致命的——RASP的理论基础(redundant structures are safely removable for SFT)没有per-structure evidence支撑。\\n\\nWorst档下，F(h)（CKA-based functional redundancy）与recovery后的activation change几乎无correlation (r=0.12)。Mixed-effects model中F(h)不显著(p=0.31)，且解释方差仅1.4%——远低于简单的weight norm (8%)或gradient importance (11%)。这demolishes CKA作为'predicting recoverability'的诊断工具的claim。如果functional redundancy不predict recoverability，Redundancy-Stability Tradeoff的机制基础就不存在。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"SFT-only Recovery Comparison\",\n    \"description\": \"Same pruned models (RASP_20, Standard_20), SFT only, same data budget. Tests recovery paradigm interaction.\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"sft_rasp_20_accuracy\": 0.6149,\n      \"sft_standard_20_accuracy\": 0.5929,\n      \"sft_gap_pp\": 2.2,\n      \"sft_gap_p_value\": 0.25,\n      \"sft_rasp_loss_curve_final\": 0.64,\n      \"sft_standard_loss_curve_final\": 0.64\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: SFT-only recovery (N=1319)\",\n        \"rows\": [\n          {\n            \"method\": \"RASP-20%\",\n            \"sft_accuracy\": \"61.49%\",\n            \"sft_loss\": \"0.64\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"method\": \"Standard-20%\",\n            \"sft_accuracy\": \"59.29%\",\n            \"sft_loss\": \"0.64\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"method\": \"Gap\",\n            \"delta\": \"+2.20pp\",\n            \"p_value\": \"0.25\"\n          }\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"SFT gap不显著。Worst档叙事：无法claim RASP对SFT recovery有advantage，因此Redundancy-Stability Tradeoff的一侧(SFT favors RASP)不成立。\\n\\n这个实验实际上已经完成（plan_002的SFT就是SFT-only recovery）。Worst档下结果不变：RASP 61.49% vs Standard 59.29%，gap 2.2pp, p=0.25。Loss curves几乎identical（都converge到0.64）。不显著的SFT gap意味着'CKA-aware pruning benefits SFT recovery'这个claim不成立。如果SFT gap都不存在，Redundancy-Stability Tradeoff（SFT favors removing redundancy, RLVR needs it）的SFT侧就是null。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"25% Sparsity RASP + Standard Full Pipeline\",\n    \"description\": \"25% sparsity: prune → eval → SFT → GRPO for both RASP and Standard\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"rasp_25_post_prune_accuracy\": 0.21,\n      \"standard_25_post_prune_accuracy\": 0.16,\n      \"rasp_25_sft_accuracy\": 0.52,\n      \"standard_25_sft_accuracy\": 0.5125,\n      \"sft_gap_25_pp\": 0.75,\n      \"sft_gap_25_p_value\": 0.35,\n      \"grpo_rasp_25_collapse_step\": 4,\n      \"grpo_standard_25_collapse_step\": 6,\n      \"grpo_rasp_25_peak_reward\": 0.011,\n      \"grpo_standard_25_peak_reward\": 0.015,\n      \"grpo_rasp_25_final_frac_zero_std\": 0.98,\n      \"grpo_standard_25_final_frac_zero_std\": 0.96,\n      \"collapse_ratio_rasp_vs_standard\": 0.67\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: 25% sparsity pipeline comparison\",\n        \"rows\": [\n          {\n            \"stage\": \"Post-prune\",\n            \"rasp_25\": \"21%\",\n            \"standard_25\": \"16%\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"stage\": \"Post-SFT\",\n            \"rasp_25\": \"52%\",\n            \"standard_25\": \"51.25%\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"stage\": \"Post-SFT gap\",\n            \"delta\": \"+0.75pp\",\n            \"p_value\": \"0.35\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"stage\": \"GRPO collapse step\",\n            \"rasp_25\": \"~4\",\n            \"standard_25\": \"~6\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"stage\": \"GRPO final frac_zero_std\",\n            \"rasp_25\": \"0.98\",\n            \"standard_25\": \"0.96\"\n          }\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: Collapse gradient comparison across sparsity\",\n        \"rows\": [\n          {\n            \"sparsity\": \"20%\",\n            \"rasp_collapse\": \"step 10\",\n            \"standard_collapse\": \"step 60\",\n            \"ratio\": \"6.0x\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"sparsity\": \"25%\",\n            \"rasp_collapse\": \"step 4\",\n            \"standard_collapse\": \"step 6\",\n            \"ratio\": \"1.5x\"\n          }\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"25% sparsity完全消解了collapse severity gradient。两者都太脆弱无法sustain GRPO training。Reviewer会argue: '你的diagnostic只在一个sparsity点work(20%)，换个sparsity就break——这不是robust mechanism而是coincidence。' SFT gap也shrink到不显著(0.75pp, p=0.35)。Worst档核心结论：Redundancy-Stability Tradeoff在25%下不可观测。\\n\\n25%是worst档的critical sparsity。Post-prune: RASP 21% vs Standard 16%（已confirmed）。Post-SFT: RASP ~52% vs Standard ~51.25%（已有Standard数据），gap缩小到<1pp (p=0.35)——因为higher sparsity下SFT recovery能力更受限于absolute damage而非which structures were removed。GRPO: 关键——两者都在≤10步内collapse。RASP step 4, Standard step 6，ratio仅0.67（不是20%下的6x差距）。这是因为25% sparsity下两个模型的exploration capacity都已被破坏到临界值以下，collapse变成near-deterministic而非structure-dependent。Severity gradient消失——无法区分'redundancy removal causing fast collapse' vs 'general over-pruning causing universal collapse'。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"30% Sparsity Probe\",\n    \"description\": \"30% sparsity prune + eval only (no recovery) for RASP and Standard\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"rasp_30_post_prune_accuracy\": 0.08,\n      \"standard_30_post_prune_accuracy\": 0.06,\n      \"rasp_30_eos_rate\": 0.25,\n      \"standard_30_eos_rate\": 0.18,\n      \"gap_pp\": 2.0,\n      \"p_value\": 0.55\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: 30% sparsity post-prune\",\n        \"rows\": [\n          {\n            \"method\": \"RASP-30%\",\n            \"accuracy\": \"8%\",\n            \"eos_rate\": \"25%\",\n            \"avg_len\": \"3200\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"method\": \"Standard-30%\",\n            \"accuracy\": \"6%\",\n            \"eos_rate\": \"18%\",\n            \"avg_len\": \"3500\"\n          }\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Confirms sparsity ceiling但对method comparison无价值。在worst档下用作evidence that structured pruning has narrow useful range (practical limitation)。\\n\\n30% sparsity下两者都接近complete collapse (8% vs 6%)。Model基本无法生成coherent reasoning。Gap 2pp在这个regime下meaningless——两者都是catastrophically damaged。这confirms 25-30%是DeepSeek-R1-Distill-Qwen-7B structured pruning的hard ceiling，但不提供任何method-differentiating evidence。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Extended Evaluation (MMLU, HumanEval, MATH-500)\",\n    \"description\": \"Best recovered config on OOD benchmarks\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"rasp_20_sft_mmlu\": 0.48,\n      \"rasp_20_sft_humaneval\": 0.35,\n      \"rasp_20_sft_math500\": 0.28,\n      \"standard_20_sft_mmlu\": 0.47,\n      \"standard_20_sft_humaneval\": 0.33,\n      \"standard_20_sft_math500\": 0.26,\n      \"unpruned_sft_mmlu\": 0.62,\n      \"unpruned_sft_humaneval\": 0.55,\n      \"unpruned_sft_math500\": 0.52,\n      \"rasp_vs_standard_mmlu_p\": 0.62,\n      \"rasp_vs_standard_humaneval_p\": 0.45,\n      \"rasp_vs_standard_math500_p\": 0.38\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: Extended evaluation\",\n        \"rows\": [\n          {\n            \"benchmark\": \"MMLU\",\n            \"unpruned\": \"62%\",\n            \"rasp_20\": \"48%\",\n            \"standard_20\": \"47%\",\n            \"gap_pp\": \"+1pp\",\n            \"p\": \"0.62\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"benchmark\": \"HumanEval\",\n            \"unpruned\": \"55%\",\n            \"rasp_20\": \"35%\",\n            \"standard_20\": \"33%\",\n            \"gap_pp\": \"+2pp\",\n            \"p\": \"0.45\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"benchmark\": \"MATH-500\",\n            \"unpruned\": \"52%\",\n            \"rasp_20\": \"28%\",\n            \"standard_20\": \"26%\",\n            \"gap_pp\": \"+2pp\",\n            \"p\": \"0.38\"\n          }\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"RASP advantage不generalize beyond GSM8K。在worst档下这是expected——如果GSM8K上gap都不显著，OOD上更不可能significant。但pruned models的uniform degradation strengthens 'structured pruning is destructive' narrative。\\n\\nOOD benchmarks下RASP vs Standard gap同样不显著。MMLU差1pp, HumanEval差2pp, MATH差2pp——都在noise range内。这是因为SFT recovery是domain-agnostic的(teacher-forcing on GSM8K)，CKA-aware pruning的marginal structural advantage不transfer到其他tasks。Worst档下这进一步confirms RASP无meaningful advantage。同时，pruned vs unpruned的大幅drop (MATH: 52%→27%)表明structured pruning造成的reasoning能力损失是across-domain的。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Bonsai Baseline 20%\",\n    \"description\": \"Bonsai (ICML 2025) gradient-free structured pruning at 20% sparsity\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"bonsai_post_prune_accuracy\": 0.24,\n      \"bonsai_post_sft_accuracy\": 0.56,\n      \"bonsai_post_grpo_collapse_step\": 8,\n      \"bonsai_grpo_peak_reward\": 0.019,\n      \"bonsai_grpo_final_frac_zero_std\": 0.93\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: Method comparison including Bonsai\",\n        \"rows\": [\n          {\n            \"method\": \"RASP\",\n            \"post_prune\": \"31%\",\n            \"post_sft\": \"61.5%\",\n            \"grpo_collapse\": \"step 10\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"method\": \"Standard\",\n            \"post_prune\": \"27%\",\n            \"post_sft\": \"59.3%\",\n            \"grpo_collapse\": \"step 60\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"method\": \"Bonsai\",\n            \"post_prune\": \"24%\",\n            \"post_sft\": \"56%\",\n            \"grpo_collapse\": \"step 8\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"method\": \"GRASPrune\",\n            \"post_prune\": \"7%\",\n            \"post_sft\": \"41%\",\n            \"grpo_collapse\": \"step 5\"\n          }\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Bonsai数据reveals collapse speed几乎perfectly correlates with post-SFT accuracy (r≈0.95)。Worst档下reviewer会argue: 'RASP collapses fast不是因为它removed redundancy, 而是因为它happens to produce slightly lower SFT quality than Standard (61.5 vs 59.3, but at 25% the gap disappears and so does the collapse difference)。Collapse is trivially predicted by model quality, not by structural damage type。'\\n\\nBonsai是gradient-free方法，通常在structured pruning中accuracy略低于gradient-based方法。Post-prune 24% (between random 18% and Standard 27%)。Post-SFT recovery到56%——低于RASP(61.5%)和Standard(59.3%)但仍reasonable。GRPO collapse at step 8——和RASP(step 10)同量级。在worst档下，Bonsai的加入进一步demonstrates所有structured pruning的GRPO都collapse，且collapse speed和post-SFT quality正相关（trivialy: worse model = faster collapse）。不提供redundancy-specific insight。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"CKA Reliability Analysis\",\n    \"description\": \"Split-half consistency + calibration size sensitivity\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"split_half_spearman_rho\": 0.72,\n      \"cal_256_vs_512_rank_corr\": 0.78,\n      \"cal_512_vs_1024_rank_corr\": 0.85,\n      \"score_variance_across_splits\": 0.15,\n      \"top_20pct_overlap_across_splits\": 0.68\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: CKA reliability metrics\",\n        \"rows\": [\n          {\n            \"metric\": \"Split-half Spearman ρ\",\n            \"value\": \"0.72\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"metric\": \"Cal-256 vs Cal-512 rank corr\",\n            \"value\": \"0.78\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"metric\": \"Cal-512 vs Cal-1024 rank corr\",\n            \"value\": \"0.85\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"metric\": \"Top-20% set overlap (split-half)\",\n            \"value\": \"68%\"\n          }\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"CKA reliability是acceptable but not high。32% decision instability在worst档下被interpret为：RASP的marginal advantage可能just是particular calibration sample的artifact而非stable structural property。\\n\\nCKA scores本身有moderate reliability (ρ=0.72 split-half)，不算terrible但也不够high for confident structure selection。Top-20% pruned structures只有68% overlap across splits——意味着32%的pruning decisions是unstable的。Calibration size从256→512→1024确实improves (0.78→0.85)，但512 (我们用的) 仍有notable instability。Worst档下这undermines RASP scoring的reliability——如果CKA scores themselves are noisy，基于它们的pruning decision也是noisy的。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Alpha Sensitivity Ablation\",\n    \"description\": \"α ∈ {0, 0.25, 0.5, 1, 2} sweep in RASP scoring at 20% sparsity, post-prune + post-SFT eval\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"alpha_0_post_prune\": 0.27,\n      \"alpha_0_post_sft\": 0.64,\n      \"alpha_0p25_post_prune\": 0.23,\n      \"alpha_0p25_post_sft\": 0.58,\n      \"alpha_0p5_post_prune\": 0.22,\n      \"alpha_0p5_post_sft\": 0.55,\n      \"alpha_1p0_post_prune\": 0.31,\n      \"alpha_1p0_post_sft\": 0.57,\n      \"alpha_2p0_post_prune\": 0.36,\n      \"alpha_2p0_post_sft\": 0.62,\n      \"optimal_alpha_post_prune\": 2.0,\n      \"optimal_alpha_post_sft\": 0.0,\n      \"correlation_postprune_vs_postsft\": -0.45\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: Alpha ablation full pipeline\",\n        \"rows\": [\n          {\n            \"alpha\": \"0.0 (=Standard)\",\n            \"post_prune\": \"27%\",\n            \"post_sft\": \"64%\",\n            \"post_sft_ci\": \"±4.7%\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"alpha\": \"0.25\",\n            \"post_prune\": \"23%\",\n            \"post_sft\": \"58%\",\n            \"post_sft_ci\": \"±4.9%\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"alpha\": \"0.5\",\n            \"post_prune\": \"22%\",\n            \"post_sft\": \"55%\",\n            \"post_sft_ci\": \"±5.0%\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"alpha\": \"1.0 (=RASP)\",\n            \"post_prune\": \"31%\",\n            \"post_sft\": \"57%\",\n            \"post_sft_ci\": \"±5.0%\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"alpha\": \"2.0\",\n            \"post_prune\": \"36%\",\n            \"post_sft\": \"62%\",\n            \"post_sft_ci\": \"±4.9%\"\n          }\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"α ablation是worst档最damaging的实验。Post-prune accuracy和post-SFT accuracy decouple——CKA optimization of post-prune is a wrong objective。α=0 (no CKA, Standard) achieves highest post-SFT despite lowest post-prune。RASP's core insight ('remove redundant structures because they're safely recoverable') is empirically falsified: recovering redundant-structure-preserving models is NOT easier。\\n\\n已有post-prune数据(α=0:27%, α=0.25:23%, α=0.5:22%, α=1:31%, α=2:36%)。Post-SFT数据在worst档下shows反转：α=0(即Standard，无CKA)给出最高post-SFT(64%)，而α=2(强CKA weighting, 最高post-prune)给出62%。α和post-SFT accuracy无单调关系，且post-prune和post-SFT accuracy negatively correlated (r=-0.45)——高post-prune不predict高post-SFT。这is devastating: RASP的CKA modulation optimizes wrong proxy。保留high-CKA structures helps immediate post-prune accuracy但doesn't help (甚至slightly hurts) SFT recovery。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Inference Speedup Benchmark\",\n    \"description\": \"Wall-clock latency + throughput for dense vs 20% RASP vs 20% Standard\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"dense_latency_ms_per_token\": 18.5,\n      \"rasp_20_latency_ms_per_token\": 16.2,\n      \"standard_20_latency_ms_per_token\": 16.0,\n      \"dense_throughput_tokens_per_sec\": 54.1,\n      \"rasp_20_throughput_tokens_per_sec\": 61.7,\n      \"standard_20_throughput_tokens_per_sec\": 62.5,\n      \"speedup_rasp_vs_dense\": 1.14,\n      \"speedup_standard_vs_dense\": 1.16,\n      \"memory_reduction_pct\": 18.5\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: Inference efficiency\",\n        \"rows\": [\n          {\n            \"model\": \"Dense (7.6B)\",\n            \"latency_ms\": \"18.5\",\n            \"throughput\": \"54.1 tok/s\",\n            \"memory_gb\": \"15.2\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"model\": \"RASP-20% (6.2B)\",\n            \"latency_ms\": \"16.2\",\n            \"throughput\": \"61.7 tok/s\",\n            \"memory_gb\": \"12.4\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"model\": \"Standard-20% (6.2B)\",\n            \"latency_ms\": \"16.0\",\n            \"throughput\": \"62.5 tok/s\",\n            \"memory_gb\": \"12.4\"\n          }\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Inference speedup insufficient to justify accuracy cost。Worst档下这weaken practical motivation：如果structured pruning只给14% speedup with 25% accuracy loss，research question本身的relevance被questioned。需要在paper中reframe为'studying fundamental interaction'而非'practical compression method'。\\n\\n20% structured pruning只给14-16% speedup。这是因为：(1) MLP-only pruning (attn groups未被pruned) 限制了speedup ceiling; (2) GPU利用率在batch_size=1时不是memory-bound; (3) Structured pruning的实际speedup远低于theoretical FLOP reduction (20%)因为kernel launch overhead和memory bandwidth不是线性关系。Worst档下1.14-1.16x speedup is disappointing——不足以justify 20pp+ accuracy loss (81%→61%)。Reviewer: 'you lose 20pp accuracy for 14% speedup — no practitioner would make this trade。'\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Unstructured Pruning Baseline 20%\",\n    \"description\": \"Magnitude-based unstructured pruning at 20%, eval + SFT → GRPO\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"unstructured_20_post_prune_accuracy\": 0.72,\n      \"unstructured_20_post_sft_accuracy\": 0.79,\n      \"unstructured_20_grpo_accuracy\": 0.79,\n      \"unstructured_20_grpo_collapse\": false,\n      \"unstructured_20_grpo_steps_stable\": 100,\n      \"unstructured_20_grpo_final_reward\": 0.55\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: Structured vs Unstructured comparison\",\n        \"rows\": [\n          {\n            \"method\": \"Dense\",\n            \"post_prune\": \"81%\",\n            \"post_sft\": \"81%\",\n            \"grpo_collapse\": \"No\",\n            \"grpo_accuracy\": \"81%\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"method\": \"Unstructured-20%\",\n            \"post_prune\": \"72%\",\n            \"post_sft\": \"79%\",\n            \"grpo_collapse\": \"No\",\n            \"grpo_accuracy\": \"79%\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"method\": \"RASP-Structured-20%\",\n            \"post_prune\": \"31%\",\n            \"post_sft\": \"61.5%\",\n            \"grpo_collapse\": \"Step 10\",\n            \"grpo_accuracy\": \"60.7%\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"method\": \"Standard-Structured-20%\",\n            \"post_prune\": \"27%\",\n            \"post_sft\": \"59.3%\",\n            \"grpo_collapse\": \"Step 60\",\n            \"grpo_accuracy\": \"58.9%\"\n          }\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Unstructured doesn't collapse → GRPO failure是structured-pruning-specific。Worst档下reviewer会reframe为capacity argument: 'structured pruning removes 20% of architecture but >>20% of effective capacity (因为removes entire functional units)，collapse是trivially因为model太弱not因为any specific structural property'。这undermines Redundancy-Stability Tradeoff的mechanistic claim进一步。\\n\\nUnstructured pruning at 20% preserves大部分accuracy (72% post-prune vs structured 27-31%)因为individual weight zeroing比removing entire structures damage far less。Post-SFT recovery到79%接近dense baseline (81%)。关键：GRPO在unstructured pruned model上NOT collapse——100 steps stable, reward reaches 0.55。这directly refutes 'pruning breaks RLVR'的general claim，narrowing it to'STRUCTURED pruning breaks RLVR'。In worst档: 这是double-edged。一方面narrows scope (only structured matters)；另一方面reviewer可能argue 'if unstructured doesn't collapse, your finding is about model capacity, not redundancy — 20% structured removes much more effective capacity than 20% unstructured'。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"SFT OOD Eval Contingency\",\n    \"description\": \"Standard SFT-recovered model (64%→59.3% GSM8K) on MATH-500 and HumanEval\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"standard_sft_math500\": 0.22,\n      \"standard_sft_humaneval\": 0.28,\n      \"rasp_sft_math500\": 0.24,\n      \"rasp_sft_humaneval\": 0.3,\n      \"unpruned_sft_math500\": 0.52,\n      \"unpruned_sft_humaneval\": 0.55,\n      \"gap_math500_pp\": 2.0,\n      \"gap_humaneval_pp\": 2.0,\n      \"gap_math500_p\": 0.35,\n      \"gap_humaneval_p\": 0.4\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: OOD evaluation\",\n        \"rows\": [\n          {\n            \"benchmark\": \"MATH-500\",\n            \"unpruned\": \"52%\",\n            \"rasp_20\": \"24%\",\n            \"standard_20\": \"22%\",\n            \"p_value\": \"0.35\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"benchmark\": \"HumanEval\",\n            \"unpruned\": \"55%\",\n            \"rasp_20\": \"30%\",\n            \"standard_20\": \"28%\",\n            \"p_value\": \"0.40\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"benchmark\": \"GSM8K\",\n            \"unpruned\": \"81%\",\n            \"rasp_20\": \"61.5%\",\n            \"standard_20\": \"59.3%\",\n            \"p_value\": \"0.25\"\n          }\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"OOD collapse suggests SFT recovery是GSM8K-specific memorization。Worst档下这weakens 'SFT-only recovery as practical recommendation'——如果SFT只恢复in-domain performance，recommendation的practical scope极其有限。\\n\\nOOD evaluation下RASP vs Standard gap同样tiny (2pp, p>0.35)。两个pruned models在harder benchmarks上都heavily degraded vs unpruned (MATH: 22-24% vs 52%, HumanEval: 28-30% vs 55%)。这表明SFT recovery在GSM8K-domain外效果很差——recovery是domain-specific pattern memorization而非genuine reasoning restoration。Worst档下这进一步削弱SFT recovery作为practical solution的framing，但不directly影响GRPO failure narrative。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Qwen-Math-7B RASP/Standard 20% SFT Eval\",\n    \"description\": \"Qwen2.5-Math-7B pruned at 20% (RASP + Standard), SFT recovery, N=200 eval\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"rasp_20_qwen_sft_accuracy\": 0.725,\n      \"standard_20_qwen_sft_accuracy\": 0.71,\n      \"gap_pp\": 1.5,\n      \"gap_p_value\": 0.42\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: Cross-model 20% SFT\",\n        \"rows\": [\n          {\n            \"model\": \"DeepSeek-R1-Distill-Qwen-7B\",\n            \"rasp\": \"61.5%\",\n            \"standard\": \"59.3%\",\n            \"gap\": \"+2.2pp\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"model\": \"Qwen2.5-Math-7B\",\n            \"rasp\": \"72.5%\",\n            \"standard\": \"71.0%\",\n            \"gap\": \"+1.5pp\"\n          }\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Cross-model SFT gap even smaller。RASP advantage不robust across models。\\n\\n已有实验数据: RASP 72.5% vs Standard 71%。Gap仅1.5pp (p=0.42)——比DeepSeek-R1上的2.2pp还小。Cross-model下CKA-aware pruning的advantage进一步diminish，因为Qwen-Math的architecture redundancy pattern可能不同于DeepSeek-R1-Distill。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Qwen-Math-7B RASP/Standard 25% Full Pipeline\",\n    \"description\": \"Qwen2.5-Math-7B pruned at 25% (RASP + Standard), SFT + GRPO, N=200 eval\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"rasp_25_qwen_sft_accuracy\": 0.64,\n      \"standard_25_qwen_sft_accuracy\": 0.63,\n      \"sft_gap_pp\": 1.0,\n      \"sft_gap_p_value\": 0.48,\n      \"grpo_rasp_25_qwen_collapse_step\": 7,\n      \"grpo_standard_25_qwen_collapse_step\": 8,\n      \"grpo_rasp_25_qwen_peak_reward\": 0.022,\n      \"grpo_standard_25_qwen_peak_reward\": 0.025,\n      \"collapse_ratio\": 0.875\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: Qwen-Math 25% GRPO collapse comparison\",\n        \"rows\": [\n          {\n            \"model\": \"DeepSeek-R1 25%\",\n            \"rasp_collapse\": \"step 4\",\n            \"standard_collapse\": \"step 6\",\n            \"ratio\": \"1.5x\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"model\": \"Qwen-Math 25%\",\n            \"rasp_collapse\": \"step 7\",\n            \"standard_collapse\": \"step 8\",\n            \"ratio\": \"1.14x\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"model\": \"DeepSeek-R1 20%\",\n            \"rasp_collapse\": \"step 10\",\n            \"standard_collapse\": \"step 60\",\n            \"ratio\": \"6.0x\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"model\": \"Qwen-Math 20%\",\n            \"rasp_collapse\": \"TBD\",\n            \"standard_collapse\": \"TBD\",\n            \"ratio\": \"TBD\"\n          }\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Cross-model non-reproducibility是worst档的killshot for mechanism claim。如果collapse gradient只在one model × one sparsity下observe，它不是generalizable mechanism而是coincidence。\\n\\nWorst档核心: Qwen-Math上GRPO collapse差异消失。RASP step 7 vs Standard step 8——ratio 0.875 (within noise)。两者都rapidly collapse，无severity gradient。这directly falsifies 'collapse speed diagnoses structural damage type' claim跨模型。原因：Qwen-Math的internal redundancy structure可能不同(more uniform, less exploitable by CKA)，或25% sparsity对Qwen-Math已经是critical threshold (Qwen-Math baseline更高所以25% damage也更severe in relative terms)。\"\n  }\n]","numLines":807,"startLine":1,"totalLines":807}}}
